1
00:00:04,903 --> 00:00:07,302
♪ In the not-too-distant future ♪

2
00:00:07,302 --> 00:00:10,811
♪ Next Sunday A.D. ♪

3
00:00:10,811 --> 00:00:13,571
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

4
00:00:13,571 --> 00:00:16,929
♪ Not too different than you or me ♪

5
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:19,908
♪ He worked in a satellite loading bay ♪

6
00:00:19,908 --> 00:00:23,158
♪ Just polishing switches to pay his way ♪

7
00:00:23,158 --> 00:00:26,108
♪ He did his job well
with a cheerful face ♪

8
00:00:26,108 --> 00:00:27,703
♪ But his bosses didn't like him ♪

9
00:00:27,703 --> 00:00:32,668
♪ So they shot him into space ♪

10
00:00:32,668 --> 00:00:35,795
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:35,795 --> 00:00:39,044
♪ The worst ever made ♪

12
00:00:39,044 --> 00:00:41,996
♪ Joel says when you got lemons ♪

13
00:00:41,996 --> 00:00:45,246
♪ You make lemonade ♪

14
00:00:45,246 --> 00:00:48,046
♪ Now keep in mind he can't control ♪

15
00:00:48,046 --> 00:00:51,516
♪ Where the movies begin or end ♪

16
00:00:51,516 --> 00:00:54,534
♪ Because he used the extra parts ♪

17
00:00:54,534 --> 00:00:59,334
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

18
00:00:59,334 --> 00:01:01,114
♪ Robot Roll Call ♪

19
00:01:01,114 --> 00:01:02,636
♪ Cambot ♪

20
00:01:02,636 --> 00:01:04,069
♪ Servo ♪

21
00:01:04,069 --> 00:01:05,631
♪ Gypsy ♪

22
00:01:05,631 --> 00:01:06,868
♪ Crow ♪

23
00:01:06,868 --> 00:01:10,221
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

24
00:01:10,221 --> 00:01:13,233
♪ And other science facts ♪

25
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:16,153
♪ Just repeat to yourself,
"It's just a show ♪

26
00:01:16,153 --> 00:01:19,366
♪ I should really just relax" ♪

27
00:01:19,366 --> 00:01:23,783
♪ For "Mystery Science Theater 3000" ♪

28
00:01:27,785 --> 00:01:30,452
(doors closing)

29
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:36,370
- All right, hey, thanks for coming

30
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:39,230
to "Mystery Science Theater
3000," I'm Joel Hodgson.

31
00:01:39,230 --> 00:01:41,770
The guys at the station
sent me this facsimile

32
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:44,980
that the next film is called
"Invaders From the Deep."

33
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:47,670
I don't know what should
upset these people so much

34
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:48,980
that they would need to invade

35
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:51,680
or what it is they're in that's so deep.

36
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,930
Cambot, could you bring
that in a little bit?

37
00:01:54,917 --> 00:01:56,270
Yeah, that's good.

38
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:59,150
And it's a Gene and Sylvia Anderson film.

39
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:01,840
They're the same people
that did "Fireball XL5,"

40
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:06,840
if you remember that, and it
stars the puppet, Troy Tempest,

41
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:10,700
and it looks like we've
got movie sign happening,

42
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:13,080
but always remember, it's
in super Marianation.

43
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,572
I'll go around, you go through.

44
00:02:14,572 --> 00:02:15,752
(alarm buzzes)

45
00:02:15,752 --> 00:02:18,419
(doors opening)

46
00:02:23,425 --> 00:02:26,175
(dramatic music)

47
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,287
(mysterious music)

48
00:02:39,109 --> 00:02:41,609
(tense music)

49
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,970
- We are constantly losing
battles to the land people.

50
00:02:51,970 --> 00:02:54,730
Battles we would win if it were not

51
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:57,417
for the World Aquanaut Security Patrol.

52
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,513
- Oh, great Typhoon.

53
00:03:03,570 --> 00:03:07,290
Show your face to Titan, leader

54
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:10,074
of the underwater city of Titanica.

55
00:03:10,074 --> 00:03:12,882
(dramatic music)

56
00:03:12,882 --> 00:03:14,703
All-powerful Typhoon.

57
00:03:15,553 --> 00:03:18,260
Vengeance must be mine.

58
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:20,400
Only Marineville stands in our way

59
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,614
of a great and glorious victory.

60
00:03:22,614 --> 00:03:25,009
(mysterious music)

61
00:03:25,009 --> 00:03:29,176
All my subjects, your
orders, destroy Marineville.

62
00:03:31,136 --> 00:03:32,493
(eerie music)

63
00:03:32,493 --> 00:03:35,493
(explosion booming)

64
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:54,040
(dramatic music)

65
00:04:51,657 --> 00:04:54,240
(serene music)

66
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:57,920
- [Joel] Excuse me.

67
00:05:12,441 --> 00:05:15,730
- Ah, this is the life, Milly.

68
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:16,660
- Of course, Henry.

69
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:18,233
I always know what's best for you.

70
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:22,030
It's about time we got
away from noise and crowds.

71
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,290
- You're right, Milly.

72
00:05:23,290 --> 00:05:24,470
You sure are.

73
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:25,863
Being an admiral was okay-

74
00:05:25,863 --> 00:05:29,310
- Now you just relax, Henry,
we're on a beautiful island,

75
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:31,060
now just enjoy it.

76
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:34,080
- Yeah, just think, not another person

77
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:37,030
within 300 miles of us.

78
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:38,140
- Henry.

79
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:40,657
- Yeah, what is that?

80
00:05:40,657 --> 00:05:43,030
- Someone's at the window.

81
00:05:43,030 --> 00:05:44,544
- Well, how could it be?

82
00:05:44,544 --> 00:05:46,310
We're completely alone on this island.

83
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:49,440
- But I tell you, Henry, there
was someone at the window.

84
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:51,900
- Now Milly, we spent all this dough

85
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:53,720
buying ourselves a private island

86
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,526
so we could be alone and lead a-

87
00:05:55,526 --> 00:05:56,750
- Henry!

88
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:57,920
It's there again.

89
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:01,100
- All right, all right, Milly, calm down.

90
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:04,113
Now, let's take a look outside.

91
00:06:09,848 --> 00:06:12,598
(waves crashing)

92
00:06:16,386 --> 00:06:18,160
Now, what did I tell you, Milly?

93
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,163
No one there.

94
00:06:20,376 --> 00:06:21,710
- [Joel] Sure.

95
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:25,130
- The window a strange unearthly face.

96
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:26,203
Be careful, Henry.

97
00:06:26,203 --> 00:06:29,199
- All right, Milly, all right.

98
00:06:29,199 --> 00:06:31,699
(tense music)

99
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,753
Milly, take a look at this.

100
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:44,620
- Well, what did I say, Henry?

101
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:47,073
I knew that there was someone.

102
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:49,387
- Just keep close by me, Milly.

103
00:06:49,387 --> 00:06:51,887
(tense music)

104
00:06:56,454 --> 00:06:58,013
- [Joel] Lettuce Man.

105
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:01,693
- Turn round very slowly.

106
00:07:03,550 --> 00:07:05,120
- Oh, Henry!

107
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:08,618
- Make a foolish move and
I will destroy you both.

108
00:07:08,618 --> 00:07:09,451
- Henry!

109
00:07:09,451 --> 00:07:10,583
- Hush, Milly.

110
00:07:10,583 --> 00:07:13,720
Do just as he says, he means business.

111
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:16,800
- I am Gadeth, the enemy of you

112
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,790
and all the accursed terrainians.

113
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:22,897
My mission is to destroy Troy Tempest

114
00:07:22,897 --> 00:07:27,482
and capture Stingray, and you
are going to help, Admiral.

115
00:07:27,482 --> 00:07:28,673
- [Man On Loudspeaker] Attention.

116
00:07:28,673 --> 00:07:33,290
Stingray crew to report to
control tower immediately.

117
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:35,760
- Seems it came from Admiral Carson.

118
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,670
- Didn't he retire a year or two back?

119
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:38,880
- Right.

120
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,800
Bought an island in the Pacific.

121
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:41,957
Now here's the message.

122
00:07:41,957 --> 00:07:43,510
"Lives in danger.

123
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:45,850
Request Stingray's aid immediately.

124
00:07:45,850 --> 00:07:47,557
Proceed with vigor."

125
00:07:47,557 --> 00:07:48,640
- "Proceed with vigor?"

126
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:51,320
Say, that's the WASP
code to warn of a trap.

127
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,210
- [Commander] Right again.

128
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:53,623
- I guess it means there's more to it

129
00:07:53,623 --> 00:07:55,170
than just to call for help.

130
00:07:55,170 --> 00:07:56,370
- You betcha.

131
00:07:56,370 --> 00:07:58,060
This is a full-scale emergency.

132
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,310
- We're on our way, Commander.

133
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,900
- Okay, Troy.

134
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,750
Now you'll need someone
who knows the country.

135
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,219
Better take Marina.

136
00:08:04,219 --> 00:08:06,719
(tense music)

137
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,560
- [Joel] She's fine.

138
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,960
- Okay, Marina?

139
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:14,858
Stingray crew standing by
at action stations, Control.

140
00:08:14,858 --> 00:08:17,358
(tense music)

141
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,860
- All right, Atlanta.

142
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:22,130
Sound launch stations.

143
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:22,963
- [Atlanta] Yes sir.

144
00:08:22,963 --> 00:08:26,130
(tense music)

145
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:27,750
- Here we go.

146
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:29,398
Just sit tight, Marina.

147
00:08:29,398 --> 00:08:31,898
(tense music)

148
00:08:47,548 --> 00:08:50,298
(dramatic music)

149
00:09:11,416 --> 00:09:13,960
- Stingray launch stage one complete, sir.

150
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,180
- Right, Atlanta.

151
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:17,890
In view of that code message,
we ought to be prepared

152
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:20,606
for an attack on Marineville.
- Yes, sir.

153
00:09:20,606 --> 00:09:21,870
- [Man On Loudspeaker] Attention.

154
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:24,080
This is Marineville Control.

155
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:27,120
All personnel stand by
for battle stations.

156
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:30,150
(dramatic music)

157
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:31,257
- Tower from Stingray.

158
00:09:31,257 --> 00:09:32,990
Are we clear to leave, Marineville?

159
00:09:32,990 --> 00:09:34,514
- Clear to go, Stingray.

160
00:09:34,514 --> 00:09:37,990
(mysterious music)

161
00:09:37,990 --> 00:09:41,135
Tower to power plant, commence
battle stations procedure.

162
00:09:41,135 --> 00:09:43,092
- [Man On Loudspeaker] Battle
stations, battle stations,

163
00:09:43,092 --> 00:09:45,161
battle stations, BWR.

164
00:09:45,161 --> 00:09:47,661
(tense music)

165
00:10:22,150 --> 00:10:23,900
- Acceleration, grade six.

166
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:24,820
- Phase six.

167
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:26,560
- Set course for Lull.

168
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,793
Turn into green lower five.

169
00:10:30,790 --> 00:10:33,707
(mysterious music)

170
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:36,525
On course for the Island of Lull.

171
00:10:36,525 --> 00:10:39,442
(mysterious music)

172
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,130
- Good work, Admiral.

173
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:47,242
Soon Stingray will arrive in
answer to your distress signal.

174
00:10:47,242 --> 00:10:49,430
Her crew are-
- I love puppet gunplay.

175
00:10:49,430 --> 00:10:50,920
- The ship will be mine.

176
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:53,470
Now go ahead of me to my underwater craft.

177
00:10:53,470 --> 00:10:55,470
- You don't stand a chance.

178
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:57,820
Stingray will be here in an hour.

179
00:10:57,820 --> 00:11:02,820
- That means Troy Tempest has
just one hour left to live.

180
00:11:03,165 --> 00:11:04,360
(dramatic music)

181
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,870
- One hour at rate six.

182
00:11:05,870 --> 00:11:08,190
That makes the Island of Lull dead ahead.

183
00:11:08,190 --> 00:11:09,460
- Thanks, Phones.

184
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,570
Reduced to rate one.

185
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:12,133
Give me a surface video scan.

186
00:11:14,989 --> 00:11:17,906
(mysterious music)

187
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:41,130
No visible sign of trouble.

188
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:41,963
- [Joel] Not yet.

189
00:11:41,963 --> 00:11:43,530
- SBC, stand by to surface.

190
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:45,380
- Standing by.
- Right.

191
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:46,890
Blow one.
- Blow one.

192
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:48,310
- [Joel] Pull my finger.

193
00:11:48,310 --> 00:11:49,540
- We're going ashore.

194
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:51,310
Say, is that toy fish aboard?

195
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,770
- Yeah, but this is no
time for practical jokes.

196
00:11:53,770 --> 00:11:55,470
- This is no joke.

197
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:57,680
I got an idea we're going to need it.

198
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:58,680
Blow three, five, and seven.

199
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:00,342
- [Joel] And play the jazz.

200
00:12:00,342 --> 00:12:03,259
(light jazz music)

201
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,260
- We're going ashore
to investigate, Marina.

202
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:17,663
But you'll be okay here?

203
00:12:19,991 --> 00:12:22,491
(tense music)

204
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:42,343
- Good.

205
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:44,513
Stingray has arrived.

206
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:48,510
Now you're aboard my
craft, there is nothing

207
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:50,759
you can do to save them.

208
00:12:50,759 --> 00:12:53,509
(dramatic music)

209
00:12:56,039 --> 00:12:58,170
- [Joel] Levitating La-Z-Boys.

210
00:13:02,508 --> 00:13:05,008
(tense music)

211
00:13:10,489 --> 00:13:12,147
- You fiend.

212
00:13:12,147 --> 00:13:16,540
You can't just sit there and
watch them go to their deaths.

213
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,140
- But I can, Admiral.

214
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:19,380
That is my mission.

215
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:22,310
And when they are
destroyed, I will be free

216
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:24,396
to take Stingray.

217
00:13:24,396 --> 00:13:26,239
(tense music)

218
00:13:26,239 --> 00:13:27,550
- What do you make of it, Phones?

219
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:28,383
- I don't know.

220
00:13:28,383 --> 00:13:29,610
Well, the door's open.

221
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:30,640
Let's take a look.

222
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,520
- Hold it.

223
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:32,870
I'm not taking any chances.

224
00:13:32,870 --> 00:13:33,703
Bring the toy fish.

225
00:13:33,703 --> 00:13:34,536
- But Troy-

226
00:13:34,536 --> 00:13:36,871
- Do as I say, Phones, do as I say.

227
00:13:36,871 --> 00:13:37,704
(tense music)

228
00:13:37,704 --> 00:13:39,930
- [Joel] The ol' toy fish.

229
00:13:39,930 --> 00:13:44,180
- Just a few minutes, and
Troy Tempest will be no more.

230
00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:48,350
- Henry, you must stop him.

231
00:13:48,350 --> 00:13:51,440
- Quiet, Milly, the WASPs
know what they're doing.

232
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,810
- I sure hope you know
what you're doing, Troy.

233
00:13:53,810 --> 00:13:54,950
- That makes two of us.

234
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:56,713
Okay, here we go.

235
00:13:57,625 --> 00:14:00,776
(motor whirring)

236
00:14:00,776 --> 00:14:04,020
Now just imagine that fish is
us walking towards the house.

237
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:05,770
Let's see what would have happened.

238
00:14:06,825 --> 00:14:09,010
(tense music)

239
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:10,137
Keep down, Phones.

240
00:14:10,137 --> 00:14:13,345
(dramatic music)

241
00:14:13,345 --> 00:14:16,428
(explosions booming)

242
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:24,680
Just as I figured.

243
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:25,970
A booby trap.

244
00:14:25,970 --> 00:14:26,990
- Yeah.

245
00:14:26,990 --> 00:14:29,347
We could have walked right
into it, wasn't for you.

246
00:14:29,347 --> 00:14:31,070
- And the admiral's code.

247
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:31,903
Come on.
- And the fish.

248
00:14:31,903 --> 00:14:34,584
(dramatic music)

249
00:14:37,477 --> 00:14:40,010
- So the famous Troy Tempest is cleverer

250
00:14:40,010 --> 00:14:42,183
than I gave him credit
for, but the next time,

251
00:14:42,183 --> 00:14:43,850
I will make certain.

252
00:14:46,930 --> 00:14:47,763
- Look, Troy.

253
00:14:49,390 --> 00:14:50,300
- That's our baby.

254
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:52,750
And I reckon the Admiral and
his wife are prisoners aboard.

255
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:54,003
Let's get back to Stingray fast.

256
00:14:54,003 --> 00:14:56,753
(dramatic music)

257
00:15:03,900 --> 00:15:05,170
- [Joel] I just can't quit thinkin'

258
00:15:05,170 --> 00:15:08,731
of that little toy fish gettin' exploded.

259
00:15:08,731 --> 00:15:11,481
(dramatic music)

260
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:17,723
- Somehow Tempest must have
been warned of the trap.

261
00:15:18,810 --> 00:15:20,610
Well done, Admiral.

262
00:15:20,610 --> 00:15:22,560
But you will suffer for your foolishness.

263
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,350
- I don't scare easy.

264
00:15:24,350 --> 00:15:26,433
You don't stand a chance with Stingray.

265
00:15:26,433 --> 00:15:29,280
- But you do not know about my base.

266
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,112
There I will be safe.

267
00:15:31,112 --> 00:15:33,862
(dramatic music)

268
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:38,310
- Flood cue.

269
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:39,143
- Flood cue.

270
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:42,960
- Okay, Phones, start sound scan.

271
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,947
They've got a head start.

272
00:15:44,947 --> 00:15:47,947
(suspenseful music)

273
00:15:58,010 --> 00:16:00,070
- Green zero-zero-two.

274
00:16:00,070 --> 00:16:01,480
- Zero-zero-two.

275
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:04,480
(suspenseful music)

276
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:12,670
- Sound scan reports rock formation ahead.

277
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:15,175
- Decelerate to investigation cruise.

278
00:16:15,175 --> 00:16:18,175
(suspenseful music)

279
00:16:22,010 --> 00:16:24,350
- Red one-three-two.

280
00:16:24,350 --> 00:16:26,200
There's a tunnel entrance dead ahead.

281
00:16:32,990 --> 00:16:35,120
- Well, Phones, they must
have gone into the tunnel.

282
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,060
- Yeah.

283
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:38,620
And it's too small to take Stingray.

284
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:40,220
We could follow in the Aqua Sprite.

285
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:41,370
- [Troy] No good, Phones.

286
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:42,480
Too much noise.

287
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,840
We want to sneak up on 'em.

288
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,540
- Then there's only one answer.

289
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:49,330
Let's put on our skin
suits and use our sea bugs.

290
00:16:49,330 --> 00:16:50,700
I'll get 'em.

291
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:51,700
- Now hold it, Phones.

292
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:52,980
Not so fast.

293
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:55,120
It's too risky.

294
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:57,050
We're not certain of the
length of that tunnel,

295
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:58,970
and our air supply could give out.

296
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:01,260
- Yeah, but Skipper the
admiral and his wife,

297
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:02,410
they're in danger.

298
00:17:02,410 --> 00:17:05,603
- I know that, but we want
to stay alive to help 'em.

299
00:17:07,350 --> 00:17:09,730
We'll have to take a sonic and
figure the tunnel's length.

300
00:17:09,730 --> 00:17:10,630
Get to it, Phones.

301
00:17:12,299 --> 00:17:14,966
(sonar beeping)

302
00:17:16,369 --> 00:17:20,320
- Well, I'd say the tunnel's
about three miles long

303
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:22,043
with a cave at the end of it.

304
00:17:22,043 --> 00:17:23,077
- Well, that's it.

305
00:17:23,077 --> 00:17:24,863
The air supply would never last.

306
00:17:26,570 --> 00:17:28,650
Phones, the escape hatch.

307
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:29,630
- Marina!

308
00:17:29,630 --> 00:17:30,502
Marina!

309
00:17:30,502 --> 00:17:33,840
(suspenseful music)

310
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:34,840
She must have heard us.

311
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:35,920
She's going into the tunnel.

312
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:38,050
- I guess she figured she'd
be the only one to help

313
00:17:38,050 --> 00:17:39,880
because she can breathe underwater.

314
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,790
- Get the sea bugs.

315
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:41,623
We're going after her.

316
00:17:41,623 --> 00:17:42,620
- But we'll never make it.

317
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:44,167
- We've gotta make it.

318
00:17:44,167 --> 00:17:47,921
(explosions booming)

319
00:17:47,921 --> 00:17:50,504
(upbeat music)

320
00:18:06,705 --> 00:18:09,288
(upbeat music)

321
00:18:11,774 --> 00:18:14,774
(suspenseful music)

322
00:18:32,049 --> 00:18:33,257
Step on it, Phones.

323
00:18:33,257 --> 00:18:34,915
- Just a minute.

324
00:18:34,915 --> 00:18:36,915
There, now that does it.

325
00:18:45,793 --> 00:18:47,100
- [Joel] They stay down pretty good

326
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:48,557
for being made outta wood.

327
00:18:48,557 --> 00:18:51,057
(tense music)

328
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:38,560
- So Troy Tempest sends a
woman to fight his battles.

329
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:39,980
Come over here.

330
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:43,055
One false move and I'll fire.

331
00:19:43,055 --> 00:19:45,805
(dramatic music)

332
00:19:47,386 --> 00:19:49,886
- [Joel] Better do as he says.

333
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:54,440
- [Phones] Troy.

334
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,880
I've got trouble with my sea bug.

335
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,490
My speed's dropping.

336
00:19:58,490 --> 00:20:00,520
- [Troy] Phones, keep calm.

337
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:02,470
I'm staying with you.

338
00:20:02,470 --> 00:20:04,190
- [Phones] You go on, Troy.

339
00:20:04,190 --> 00:20:06,602
Our air won't last at this speed.

340
00:20:06,602 --> 00:20:08,220
Now that's for sure.

341
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:09,930
- [Troy] I'm staying with you, Phones.

342
00:20:09,930 --> 00:20:13,210
Just keep going at the
best speed you can get.

343
00:20:13,210 --> 00:20:15,170
- [Joel] Just let go and
let the threads drag ya.

344
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:17,020
- Now, what are Troy Tempest's plans?

345
00:20:17,870 --> 00:20:19,520
Speak, do you hear me?

346
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,030
Speak!

347
00:20:21,030 --> 00:20:23,892
- Leave her alone, you crazy fools.

348
00:20:23,892 --> 00:20:25,238
- Quiet!

349
00:20:25,238 --> 00:20:28,080
Marin, we must make the girl talk.

350
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:29,640
Fix things up at once.

351
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:31,170
- Yes, Gadeth.

352
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,227
- [Joel] He just said "lettuce."

353
00:20:33,227 --> 00:20:34,100
"Yes, lettuce."

354
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,510
See what I mean?

355
00:20:35,510 --> 00:20:36,770
Lettuce head.

356
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:38,650
- [Phones] How much further, Troy?

357
00:20:38,650 --> 00:20:40,380
My air is running low.

358
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:42,377
- [Troy] And mine, Phones.

359
00:20:42,377 --> 00:20:44,073
We've gotta keep going.

360
00:20:45,050 --> 00:20:47,870
This tunnel can't be much longer.

361
00:20:47,870 --> 00:20:49,870
- [Phones] Leave me, Troy.

362
00:20:49,870 --> 00:20:51,590
You can make it.

363
00:20:51,590 --> 00:20:56,420
- [Troy] Either we both make
it or we both don't make it.

364
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:58,791
I'm staying with you.

365
00:20:58,791 --> 00:21:01,541
(dramatic music)

366
00:21:02,925 --> 00:21:06,080
- Now talk, or you will die.

367
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,450
- [Joel] You're barking up the wrong tree.

368
00:21:07,450 --> 00:21:10,170
She can't speak, she's from underwater.

369
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:13,523
- When the flame reaches the
line, the swordfish will drop.

370
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:17,043
You have less than 10
marine minutes to speak.

371
00:21:17,961 --> 00:21:19,309
(dramatic music)

372
00:21:19,309 --> 00:21:21,309
- [Joel] Marine minutes.

373
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,493
Jack the knife.

374
00:21:26,616 --> 00:21:29,116
(tense music)

375
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:39,234
(Joel laughing)

376
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:49,623
Just cut those lines
and you can go faster.

377
00:22:04,930 --> 00:22:06,810
- [Phones] My air, Troy.

378
00:22:06,810 --> 00:22:07,643
It's finished.

379
00:22:08,710 --> 00:22:10,140
Go on.

380
00:22:10,140 --> 00:22:11,660
You'll have to leave me.

381
00:22:11,660 --> 00:22:13,440
- [Troy] Keep going, Phones.

382
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:14,323
Keep going.

383
00:22:18,069 --> 00:22:19,160
(dramatic music)

384
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:20,800
- [Joel] I think it's a
good time to point out that-

385
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,520
- [Gadeth] Five marine minutes left.

386
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:24,840
- [Joel] These puppets
do their own stunts.

387
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:26,060
- Speak!

388
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:28,527
What are Troy Tempest's plans?

389
00:22:38,608 --> 00:22:40,573
- [Troy] Phones, grab my hand.

390
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:47,775
My air's going too.

391
00:22:47,775 --> 00:22:49,108
Must keep going.

392
00:22:54,398 --> 00:22:57,148
(dramatic music)

393
00:23:02,770 --> 00:23:04,320
- [Joel] Try to reason with it.

394
00:23:25,891 --> 00:23:27,141
Still fighting.

395
00:23:28,383 --> 00:23:30,030
- Are you okay, Phones?

396
00:23:30,030 --> 00:23:30,863
- I guess so.

397
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:33,440
Thanks, Troy.

398
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:34,273
- Forget it.

399
00:23:34,273 --> 00:23:35,213
Let's go find Marina.

400
00:23:36,590 --> 00:23:37,423
- Let the girl go.

401
00:23:37,423 --> 00:23:39,330
Can't you see she knows nothing?

402
00:23:39,330 --> 00:23:41,010
- You must be crazy.

403
00:23:41,010 --> 00:23:42,100
Just crazy.

404
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:43,390
- Speak, girl!

405
00:23:43,390 --> 00:23:45,400
You have less than two minutes.

406
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:47,580
Troy Tempest sent to you here alone.

407
00:23:47,580 --> 00:23:49,820
He was willing to risk your life.

408
00:23:49,820 --> 00:23:51,620
He doesn't care about you.

409
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:52,800
- Don't move, anyone.

410
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:53,950
- Tempest.

411
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:55,621
- Release her or we fire.

412
00:23:55,621 --> 00:24:00,621
(dramatic music)
(gunshots banging)

413
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,220
We gotta stop that candle burning.

414
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:09,053
(Joel laughing)

415
00:24:09,053 --> 00:24:10,650
(gunshots banging)

416
00:24:10,650 --> 00:24:13,650
(suspenseful music)

417
00:24:19,813 --> 00:24:21,120
Have to draw their fire.

418
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:22,480
- That means me, Troy.

419
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,906
Better shot than I am, anyway.

420
00:24:23,906 --> 00:24:26,823
(gunshots banging)

421
00:24:30,921 --> 00:24:32,071
(suspenseful music)

422
00:24:32,071 --> 00:24:34,680
(explosion booms)

423
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:36,390
- We haven't got time to
play this cool, Phones.

424
00:24:36,390 --> 00:24:38,240
When I give the word, dive into the open

425
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,445
and blast that rock!

426
00:24:39,445 --> 00:24:44,445
(gunshots banging)
(suspenseful music)

427
00:24:46,939 --> 00:24:47,772
Now!

428
00:24:48,651 --> 00:24:51,901
- [Joel] I love the way that guy moves.

429
00:24:52,997 --> 00:24:55,497
(Joel laughs)

430
00:24:58,355 --> 00:25:01,850
(explosion booming)

431
00:25:01,850 --> 00:25:02,683
- Don't shoot!

432
00:25:02,683 --> 00:25:04,077
We surrender!

433
00:25:04,077 --> 00:25:06,327
- Keep 'em covered, Phones!

434
00:25:07,529 --> 00:25:08,362
(dramatic music)

435
00:25:08,362 --> 00:25:09,440
- [Joel] And he's made out of wood, too.

436
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:10,807
You know how dangerous that is?

437
00:25:10,807 --> 00:25:11,837
- He did it!

438
00:25:11,837 --> 00:25:13,504
Troy Tempest did it!

439
00:25:16,590 --> 00:25:17,933
- Are you okay, Marina?

440
00:25:19,214 --> 00:25:21,714
(tense music)

441
00:25:22,730 --> 00:25:23,880
Don't worry.

442
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:25,813
We'll soon have you out of this.

443
00:25:33,087 --> 00:25:35,837
(dramatic music)

444
00:25:38,835 --> 00:25:40,263
- [Joel] Grr.

445
00:25:40,263 --> 00:25:42,227
- Heavens, that was a close thing.

446
00:25:42,227 --> 00:25:43,690
- All right then, Milly.

447
00:25:43,690 --> 00:25:45,480
Oh, that girl's tops.

448
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,917
They tried to make her talk-

449
00:25:46,917 --> 00:25:49,000
- But she just wouldn't
give you away, Captain.

450
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,610
- No sir, she didn't say a word.

451
00:25:51,610 --> 00:25:53,820
- Well, there's a very good
reason for that, Admiral.

452
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:55,200
- You see, she can't speak.

453
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:56,660
She doesn't know how.

454
00:25:56,660 --> 00:25:59,963
And even if she could, I know
she wouldn't have let us down.

455
00:26:00,930 --> 00:26:02,013
Am I right, Marina?

456
00:26:03,462 --> 00:26:04,420
(dramatic music)

457
00:26:04,420 --> 00:26:05,793
- Oh, she says that now.

458
00:26:08,026 --> 00:26:10,693
(alarm blaring)

459
00:26:12,875 --> 00:26:14,134
- [Man On Loudspeaker] Attention.

460
00:26:14,134 --> 00:26:15,974
Marineville tracking station calling.

461
00:26:15,974 --> 00:26:18,600
Missile approaching, impact 30 seconds!

462
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:20,077
- Emergency battle stations!

463
00:26:20,077 --> 00:26:22,547
- [Atlanta] Power plant, battle stations.

464
00:26:22,547 --> 00:26:25,547
(suspenseful music)

465
00:26:42,213 --> 00:26:44,213
- Fire WASP interceptor!

466
00:26:47,761 --> 00:26:51,051
(suspenseful music)

467
00:26:51,051 --> 00:26:54,051
(explosion booming)

468
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,720
Tower to tracking station.

469
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:59,030
Imperative source of missiles located.

470
00:26:59,030 --> 00:26:59,969
- [Man On Intercom] Approximate location

471
00:26:59,969 --> 00:27:01,350
undersea, Commander.

472
00:27:01,350 --> 00:27:03,800
Position South-Southwest 1800.

473
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:06,520
References 20, 21, and 22.

474
00:27:06,520 --> 00:27:08,143
- That's a 200-mile radius.

475
00:27:09,090 --> 00:27:10,410
Can't you get any closer than that?

476
00:27:10,410 --> 00:27:11,480
- [Man On Intercom] Negative, sir.

477
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:13,240
Only approximate position available.

478
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,169
- Okay, tracking station.

479
00:27:15,169 --> 00:27:17,400
Alert jet squadron, and Stingray, Atlanta.

480
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,430
I want that area searched.

481
00:27:18,430 --> 00:27:19,349
- [Atlanta] Yes sir.

482
00:27:19,349 --> 00:27:22,099
(dramatic music)

483
00:27:24,570 --> 00:27:26,670
- Tower from Stingray, seaborne.

484
00:27:26,670 --> 00:27:28,040
- Okay, Troy

485
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:31,000
Proceed at full speed to
position South-Southwest,

486
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,870
1800 reference 20, 22.

487
00:27:33,870 --> 00:27:35,970
Thorough search of area vital.

488
00:27:35,970 --> 00:27:37,120
Priority one.

489
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:38,030
- Okay, sir.

490
00:27:38,030 --> 00:27:39,457
We're on our way.

491
00:27:39,457 --> 00:27:41,719
- [Man On Loudspeaker]
Central control to jet squad.

492
00:27:41,719 --> 00:27:42,552
Scramble.

493
00:27:43,770 --> 00:27:46,687
(engines rumbling)

494
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:12,930
- Approaching the search area, Troy.

495
00:28:12,930 --> 00:28:14,020
- Okay, Phones.

496
00:28:14,020 --> 00:28:15,750
Start sound scan.

497
00:28:15,750 --> 00:28:18,417
(sonar beeping)

498
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,900
- Area reference 20 negative.

499
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:29,850
- Right.

500
00:28:29,850 --> 00:28:31,300
Moving to area 21.

501
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:32,380
- [Joel] Not area 21.

502
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:35,977
(sonar beeping)

503
00:28:42,196 --> 00:28:43,779
- Area 21 negative.

504
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:46,721
Apart from an island, that is.

505
00:28:46,721 --> 00:28:49,471
(dramatic music)

506
00:28:50,764 --> 00:28:53,681
(engines rumbling)

507
00:29:04,780 --> 00:29:05,820
- Okay, Phones.

508
00:29:05,820 --> 00:29:06,860
Standby to surface.

509
00:29:06,860 --> 00:29:08,370
We'll check it out.

510
00:29:08,370 --> 00:29:09,690
Blow one.

511
00:29:09,690 --> 00:29:10,822
- [Joel] Pull my finger

512
00:29:10,822 --> 00:29:13,739
(mysterious music)

513
00:29:22,172 --> 00:29:24,589
- Can you see anything, Troy?

514
00:29:25,893 --> 00:29:27,703
- [Joel] Just a low-budget island.

515
00:29:30,860 --> 00:29:33,480
- No, phones, this island's deserted.

516
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:35,593
That missile couldn't
have come from there.

517
00:29:37,198 --> 00:29:39,290
(Joel mumbling)

518
00:29:39,290 --> 00:29:41,430
- I guess we better check out area 22.

519
00:29:41,430 --> 00:29:43,123
There's nothing here.

520
00:29:44,090 --> 00:29:46,190
- Hmm, doesn't seem to be.

521
00:29:46,190 --> 00:29:47,420
How about you, Marina?

522
00:29:47,420 --> 00:29:48,683
You see anything?

523
00:29:49,870 --> 00:29:50,703
- [Joel] She can't talk.

524
00:29:50,703 --> 00:29:52,153
- Okay, that's it, then.

525
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:56,250
Tower from Stingray,
areas 20 and 21 negative.

526
00:29:56,250 --> 00:29:58,161
Proceeding to area 22.

527
00:29:58,161 --> 00:30:00,744
(solemn music)

528
00:30:02,668 --> 00:30:05,418
(dramatic music)

529
00:30:07,063 --> 00:30:08,670
Tower from Stingray.

530
00:30:08,670 --> 00:30:10,740
Missile launched from island in area 21.

531
00:30:10,740 --> 00:30:12,010
- Fire WASP interceptor!

532
00:30:12,010 --> 00:30:12,863
- Yes, sir.

533
00:30:12,863 --> 00:30:15,863
(suspenseful music)

534
00:30:19,186 --> 00:30:20,540
- Finish that missile
before it has a chance

535
00:30:20,540 --> 00:30:22,517
to get so close this time.

536
00:30:22,517 --> 00:30:25,517
(suspenseful music)

537
00:30:28,087 --> 00:30:31,087
(explosion booming)

538
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:36,344
Okay, Troy investigate the
island, but use extreme caution.

539
00:30:36,344 --> 00:30:39,094
(dramatic music)

540
00:30:40,819 --> 00:30:43,999
(explosions booming)

541
00:30:43,999 --> 00:30:46,666
(doors closing)

542
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:51,610
- Hey, Crow, what do you know?

543
00:30:51,610 --> 00:30:54,560
- I just got back from
Kokomo, Joel Hodgson.

544
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:56,780
- Anyway, hey Cambot,
bring it in a little bit,

545
00:30:56,780 --> 00:30:58,260
I want to show 'em this...

546
00:30:59,380 --> 00:31:02,890
I kind dabble a little bit
in genetic engineering myself

547
00:31:02,890 --> 00:31:05,610
and I invented this,
it's my interpretation

548
00:31:05,610 --> 00:31:07,193
of a man-eating plant.

549
00:31:08,506 --> 00:31:10,440
- Ooh, that's very interesting.

550
00:31:10,440 --> 00:31:13,200
- Yeah, as you know, you
can go back now, Cambot.

551
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:15,100
Anyway, as you know,
space is a great place

552
00:31:15,100 --> 00:31:16,340
to develop new ideas.

553
00:31:16,340 --> 00:31:20,150
This is my new invention
for the human race.

554
00:31:20,150 --> 00:31:23,360
And you know how they
have airbags for cars,

555
00:31:23,360 --> 00:31:25,020
but really they don't have anything

556
00:31:25,020 --> 00:31:27,513
for anybody who drives motorcycles.

557
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:29,993
So I invented this.

558
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,940
- Wow, that blows my mind.

559
00:31:32,940 --> 00:31:34,900
Being a human must be a rush.

560
00:31:34,900 --> 00:31:37,090
- Yeah, it is, it really is, Crow.

561
00:31:37,090 --> 00:31:39,330
Anyway, I think it's time to get going.

562
00:31:39,330 --> 00:31:40,398
Stay tuned.

563
00:31:40,398 --> 00:31:42,749
(Joel vocalizes)

564
00:31:42,749 --> 00:31:45,332
(upbeat music)

565
00:32:03,053 --> 00:32:05,636
(upbeat music)

566
00:32:08,530 --> 00:32:10,890
- There must be some kind
of base beneath the island.

567
00:32:10,890 --> 00:32:13,010
The easiest way to enter
would be down in the crater.

568
00:32:13,010 --> 00:32:14,010
- Yeah.

569
00:32:14,010 --> 00:32:16,170
We could meet another
missile on its way up.

570
00:32:16,170 --> 00:32:17,550
- Exactly.

571
00:32:17,550 --> 00:32:19,240
Come on, we'll dive and take a look around

572
00:32:19,240 --> 00:32:20,300
beneath the water.

573
00:32:20,300 --> 00:32:22,484
There could be another
entrance down there.

574
00:32:22,484 --> 00:32:25,484
(suspenseful music)

575
00:32:34,190 --> 00:32:35,070
Okay. Phones.

576
00:32:35,070 --> 00:32:37,870
Now keep looking for some kind of opening.

577
00:32:37,870 --> 00:32:40,870
(suspenseful music)

578
00:32:47,590 --> 00:32:49,590
- [Crow] What's happening, Joel Hodgson?

579
00:32:50,530 --> 00:32:52,370
- [Joel] Well, these lettuce guys, wait-

580
00:32:52,370 --> 00:32:53,640
- A cave mouth.

581
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,090
- Yeah.

582
00:32:55,090 --> 00:32:57,720
It could lead us to the
base of the volcano.

583
00:32:57,720 --> 00:32:58,717
Let's take a look.

584
00:32:58,717 --> 00:33:00,670
(mysterious music)

585
00:33:00,670 --> 00:33:04,310
- [Joel] Okay, well, this
one emperor guy tried to...

586
00:33:05,530 --> 00:33:06,625
- [Crow] Is he the emperor?

587
00:33:06,625 --> 00:33:08,030
- [Joel] No.

588
00:33:08,030 --> 00:33:10,707
We're gonna have to wait till the break.

589
00:33:10,707 --> 00:33:12,870
- There's a shaft above us, Troy.

590
00:33:12,870 --> 00:33:14,803
- And I can see light.

591
00:33:14,803 --> 00:33:17,080
(mysterious music)

592
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:19,190
Okay, we're going to surface, Phones.

593
00:33:19,190 --> 00:33:20,550
- Blow one.
- Blow one.

594
00:33:20,550 --> 00:33:21,633
- [Joel] Pull my finger.

595
00:33:22,655 --> 00:33:23,605
- [Crow] Blow one, I get it.

596
00:33:23,605 --> 00:33:26,093
(Crow laughing)

597
00:33:26,093 --> 00:33:29,010
(mysterious music)

598
00:33:34,016 --> 00:33:36,944
(dramatic music)

599
00:33:36,944 --> 00:33:39,861
(mysterious music)

600
00:33:50,180 --> 00:33:51,210
- Okay, Phones.

601
00:33:51,210 --> 00:33:53,230
Let's take a look at that
tunnel at the far end.

602
00:33:53,230 --> 00:33:54,350
- Right.

603
00:33:54,350 --> 00:33:56,530
- Marina, you just sit tight.

604
00:33:56,530 --> 00:33:57,987
- [Joel] Watch these things.

605
00:33:58,930 --> 00:34:00,933
Levitating La-Z-Boy recliners.

606
00:34:01,820 --> 00:34:03,767
- [Crow] I had a brother
who could do that once.

607
00:34:03,767 --> 00:34:06,793
(Crow laughing)

608
00:34:06,793 --> 00:34:09,543
(dramatic music)

609
00:34:12,670 --> 00:34:14,280
(eerie music)

610
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,767
- Troy, what's that?

611
00:34:16,693 --> 00:34:18,993
- I don't know, but I don't like it.

612
00:34:20,627 --> 00:34:23,294
(Joel chuckles)

613
00:34:25,810 --> 00:34:28,030
- [Crow] They sure are
funny-looking for humans.

614
00:34:28,030 --> 00:34:28,863
- My arm.

615
00:34:28,863 --> 00:34:30,400
- [Joel] It's a boredom ray.

616
00:34:30,400 --> 00:34:31,563
- I can't move it.

617
00:34:33,009 --> 00:34:34,040
- [Joel] A disarming ray.

618
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:35,624
- Mine either.

619
00:34:35,624 --> 00:34:36,513
It's numb.

620
00:34:41,240 --> 00:34:45,007
- It must be a paralyzing
ray of some kind.

621
00:34:45,940 --> 00:34:47,487
I can't move a muscle.

622
00:34:47,487 --> 00:34:49,987
(eerie music)

623
00:34:51,430 --> 00:34:52,263
- Troy.

624
00:34:52,263 --> 00:34:54,891
- [Joel] Are they sweating or is that sap?

625
00:34:54,891 --> 00:34:56,564
- Hardly speak.

626
00:34:56,564 --> 00:34:59,064
(eerie music)

627
00:35:00,025 --> 00:35:03,025
(suspenseful music)

628
00:35:07,660 --> 00:35:09,030
- [Crow] Forced to watch their own movie.

629
00:35:09,030 --> 00:35:10,009
How horrible.

630
00:35:10,009 --> 00:35:12,676
(Joel chuckles)

631
00:35:17,026 --> 00:35:20,050
- Welcome to our base, Captain Tempest.

632
00:35:20,050 --> 00:35:22,960
You are beneath the island Bahow.

633
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:24,190
- Who are you?

634
00:35:24,190 --> 00:35:25,310
What do you want with us?

635
00:35:25,310 --> 00:35:27,640
- All you need to know
is that we are going

636
00:35:27,640 --> 00:35:31,580
to destroy Marineville and
you are going to help us.

637
00:35:31,580 --> 00:35:32,750
- You're crazy.

638
00:35:32,750 --> 00:35:34,010
I'll never do that.

639
00:35:34,010 --> 00:35:36,940
- Ah, but you're will, Tempest.

640
00:35:36,940 --> 00:35:40,010
All we require is some information.

641
00:35:40,010 --> 00:35:41,690
- You'll get nothing outta me.

642
00:35:41,690 --> 00:35:43,280
- No sir, me neither.

643
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,113
- [Crow] I like it.

644
00:35:44,113 --> 00:35:46,350
- I know you are both brave men.

645
00:35:46,350 --> 00:35:49,419
It would be a lengthy business
trying to make you talk,

646
00:35:49,419 --> 00:35:53,330
unaided, but talk you shall.

647
00:35:53,330 --> 00:35:54,913
Show them, Chidora.

648
00:35:56,313 --> 00:35:57,146
- [Joel] Chidora?

649
00:35:57,146 --> 00:35:58,020
(mysterious music)

650
00:35:58,020 --> 00:35:59,554
Sounds like a kinda sweater.

651
00:35:59,554 --> 00:36:01,074
(tense music)

652
00:36:01,074 --> 00:36:03,741
(Crow chuckles)

653
00:36:05,950 --> 00:36:07,263
It's your mystery date.

654
00:36:08,972 --> 00:36:09,980
- [Crow] Are you ready?

655
00:36:09,980 --> 00:36:10,813
- You hear me?

656
00:36:10,813 --> 00:36:11,730
Release her.

657
00:36:11,730 --> 00:36:13,130
- Shut up and listen, Tempest.

658
00:36:13,130 --> 00:36:14,873
I want to know on what frequencies

659
00:36:14,873 --> 00:36:17,670
Marineville's interceptors work.

660
00:36:17,670 --> 00:36:18,580
- I get it.

661
00:36:18,580 --> 00:36:20,380
You'll jam the interceptors
so your rockets

662
00:36:20,380 --> 00:36:22,153
can get through and destroy Marineville.

663
00:36:22,153 --> 00:36:24,650
- Very smart, Troy Tempest.

664
00:36:24,650 --> 00:36:28,400
Now give me the information
or Marina will suffer.

665
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,933
Explain, Chidora.

666
00:36:30,906 --> 00:36:32,580
- It is simple.

667
00:36:32,580 --> 00:36:37,580
As I turn this control, the
electronic power increases.

668
00:36:38,010 --> 00:36:41,005
Marina will be quite safe until

669
00:36:41,005 --> 00:36:44,560
a thousand marine volts are reached.

670
00:36:44,560 --> 00:36:45,753
Then she will die.

671
00:36:46,940 --> 00:36:47,890
- Let her go.

672
00:36:47,890 --> 00:36:48,723
Do you hear me?

673
00:36:48,723 --> 00:36:49,640
Let her go!

674
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,270
- Certainly, Tempest.

675
00:36:51,270 --> 00:36:54,309
When I have the correct
interceptor frequencies.

676
00:36:54,309 --> 00:36:55,560
- Troy.

677
00:36:55,560 --> 00:36:59,007
If we tell him, Commander Shaw, Atlanta,

678
00:36:59,007 --> 00:37:00,850
all of Marineville will be wiped out.

679
00:37:00,850 --> 00:37:03,743
- And if we keep quiet, Marina dies.

680
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:07,522
- [Gadeth] Well, Tempest, I am waiting.

681
00:37:07,522 --> 00:37:11,070
(dramatic music)

682
00:37:11,070 --> 00:37:12,160
- No deal, fella.

683
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:14,354
It's three lives against thousands.

684
00:37:14,354 --> 00:37:16,183
- Very well.

685
00:37:16,183 --> 00:37:18,133
Chidora, the voltage.

686
00:37:22,397 --> 00:37:24,897
(tense music)

687
00:37:30,900 --> 00:37:33,140
- 300 marine volts.

688
00:37:33,140 --> 00:37:35,003
She can feel nothing yet, Tempest,

689
00:37:35,003 --> 00:37:37,265
but the power is increasing.

690
00:37:37,265 --> 00:37:39,765
(tense music)

691
00:37:51,907 --> 00:37:54,907
- [Joel] His hair's standing on end.

692
00:37:56,511 --> 00:37:59,511
- [Crow] I wouldn't know about hair.

693
00:38:00,520 --> 00:38:01,530
- [Joel] Look at him sweating.

694
00:38:01,530 --> 00:38:04,220
(tense music)

695
00:38:04,220 --> 00:38:07,163
- Only 200 marine volts to go.

696
00:38:10,670 --> 00:38:11,780
- [Crow] The lights are yellow.

697
00:38:11,780 --> 00:38:12,820
They better clear the intersection.

698
00:38:12,820 --> 00:38:14,297
- Still refuse to cooperate?

699
00:38:14,297 --> 00:38:15,130
Very well.

700
00:38:15,983 --> 00:38:17,457
Full power.

701
00:38:17,457 --> 00:38:19,273
The fatal dose!

702
00:38:20,469 --> 00:38:23,052
(solemn music)

703
00:38:32,866 --> 00:38:36,047
(dramatic music)

704
00:38:36,047 --> 00:38:37,775
- [Joel] I think she likes it.

705
00:38:37,775 --> 00:38:40,320
- [Crow] Her head must be
made of fiberglass insulation.

706
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:41,210
- I'll talk.

707
00:38:41,210 --> 00:38:43,930
- [Gadeth] Well, Tempest?

708
00:38:43,930 --> 00:38:45,830
The frequencies?

709
00:38:45,830 --> 00:38:47,403
- 2000 mega cycles.

710
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:50,223
Ultra nine-seven-five.

711
00:38:51,350 --> 00:38:52,693
Cryptic zero-zero.

712
00:38:53,610 --> 00:38:55,210
D-a-c.

713
00:38:55,210 --> 00:38:57,040
- [Crow] Joel Hodgson,
that's my frequency.

714
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:57,873
- [Joel] Yeah.

715
00:38:57,873 --> 00:38:59,340
- [Gadeth] Take them to the cell, Chidora.

716
00:38:59,340 --> 00:39:01,260
They will remain our prisoners.

717
00:39:01,260 --> 00:39:04,010
(dramatic music)

718
00:39:04,959 --> 00:39:06,343
- [Crow] Does that mean I'm in trouble?

719
00:39:06,343 --> 00:39:07,843
- [Joel] No, except the movie.

720
00:39:09,710 --> 00:39:10,543
- [Crow] Good.

721
00:39:10,543 --> 00:39:12,803
- In you go, and hurry.

722
00:39:12,803 --> 00:39:15,240
I have much work to do on the missile.

723
00:39:15,240 --> 00:39:16,440
- [Joel] I hope these two characters

724
00:39:16,440 --> 00:39:18,073
were based on Tony Randall.

725
00:39:22,780 --> 00:39:24,795
I'd like to share a cell with him.

726
00:39:24,795 --> 00:39:27,545
(dramatic music)

727
00:39:39,980 --> 00:39:41,460
- The prisoners are secure.

728
00:39:41,460 --> 00:39:42,520
- Good.

729
00:39:42,520 --> 00:39:44,783
Now we must alter our missile frequencies.

730
00:39:45,630 --> 00:39:46,740
Come, Chidora.

731
00:39:46,740 --> 00:39:47,990
- What now, Troy?

732
00:39:47,990 --> 00:39:49,020
- Quick, give me one of your buttons.

733
00:39:49,020 --> 00:39:50,250
- A button?

734
00:39:50,250 --> 00:39:51,680
Troy, have you gone crazy?

735
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:53,320
- Don't argue, Phones, we haven't time.

736
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:54,423
The button, quickly.

737
00:39:55,300 --> 00:39:57,100
- [Joel] Why doesn't he
use one of his own buttons?

738
00:39:57,100 --> 00:39:58,610
- Marina, start ripping that cushion cover

739
00:39:58,610 --> 00:39:59,582
into strips will ya?

740
00:39:59,582 --> 00:40:00,415
(Crow mumbles)

741
00:40:00,415 --> 00:40:01,248
- What's this all about?

742
00:40:01,248 --> 00:40:03,182
- [Troy] Stick around and you'll see.

743
00:40:03,182 --> 00:40:05,932
(dramatic music)

744
00:40:07,386 --> 00:40:09,403
- Now work on the new frequencies.

745
00:40:09,403 --> 00:40:12,476
This is going to be a long job, Chidora.

746
00:40:12,476 --> 00:40:15,393
(mysterious music)

747
00:40:25,700 --> 00:40:28,653
- Right, let's hope Lady
Luck of smiling at us.

748
00:40:29,660 --> 00:40:30,493
Here goes.

749
00:40:31,930 --> 00:40:33,147
- [Crow] Hopefully
she'll do more than that.

750
00:40:33,147 --> 00:40:35,943
- Now we gently pull it in.
- Crow.

751
00:40:40,594 --> 00:40:42,365
Oh!
- Missed.

752
00:40:42,365 --> 00:40:46,185
Now this time it's gonna work.

753
00:40:46,185 --> 00:40:47,976
- It's got to.
- Metric.

754
00:40:47,976 --> 00:40:49,517
17 megavolts.

755
00:40:49,517 --> 00:40:51,720
- [Joel] Why don't they just
use one of their threads.

756
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:56,210
- That means the electrostatic
gauge reads 7000 gyrometers.

757
00:40:56,210 --> 00:40:57,310
- Check.

758
00:40:57,310 --> 00:40:59,947
Increase hydraulic to three
quarters of a megacycle.

759
00:41:03,870 --> 00:41:05,820
The weather report is favorable for firing

760
00:41:05,820 --> 00:41:07,210
at first light, Nucella.

761
00:41:07,210 --> 00:41:08,220
- Good.

762
00:41:08,220 --> 00:41:10,021
The rocket will be ready.

763
00:41:10,021 --> 00:41:11,650
This time we will not fail.

764
00:41:11,650 --> 00:41:16,000
Marineville will be destroyed.

765
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:18,500
(tense music)

766
00:41:20,430 --> 00:41:21,680
- Okay, you got it, Troy.

767
00:41:21,680 --> 00:41:23,237
Now easy does it.

768
00:41:23,237 --> 00:41:25,737
(tense music)

769
00:41:27,277 --> 00:41:28,595
Has it come loose, Troy?

770
00:41:28,595 --> 00:41:30,310
- I don't know.

771
00:41:30,310 --> 00:41:31,183
We'll soon see.

772
00:41:32,060 --> 00:41:32,923
Nearly there.

773
00:41:35,830 --> 00:41:37,060
- Troy.

774
00:41:37,060 --> 00:41:38,760
I hear footsteps.

775
00:41:38,760 --> 00:41:39,593
- Right.

776
00:41:39,593 --> 00:41:42,430
(suspenseful music)

777
00:41:50,919 --> 00:41:54,040
- We are going to our
quarters now to rest, Tempest.

778
00:41:54,040 --> 00:41:56,036
- [Joel] Sure they are.

779
00:41:56,036 --> 00:41:57,500
- I believe it.
- It will be fired at dawn,

780
00:41:57,500 --> 00:41:59,970
and you will be able to
watch the destruction

781
00:41:59,970 --> 00:42:01,973
of Marineville on our monitors.

782
00:42:03,120 --> 00:42:05,233
- Nice.
- Until dawn, then.

783
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:07,670
- [Carry] I'd be tired if I had to carry

784
00:42:07,670 --> 00:42:09,088
a diving board around on my head.

785
00:42:09,088 --> 00:42:12,494
(Joel laughing)

786
00:42:12,494 --> 00:42:14,980
- Oh boy, was that close.

787
00:42:14,980 --> 00:42:17,730
I thought sure he was gonna
notice the key had gone.

788
00:42:17,730 --> 00:42:19,240
- Yeah, me too.

789
00:42:19,240 --> 00:42:21,150
I want to take a look at that missile.

790
00:42:21,150 --> 00:42:23,760
We'll wait until things quiet down.

791
00:42:23,760 --> 00:42:25,259
Then we start.

792
00:42:25,259 --> 00:42:27,759
(tense music)

793
00:42:37,069 --> 00:42:39,190
- Are you nearly through, Troy?

794
00:42:39,190 --> 00:42:40,810
It's about an hour till dawn.

795
00:42:40,810 --> 00:42:42,090
- Okay, Phones.

796
00:42:42,090 --> 00:42:44,260
I can't rush this job.

797
00:42:44,260 --> 00:42:47,460
One false move and we'll
all be blown to paradise.

798
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:48,963
- Now he tells me.

799
00:42:48,963 --> 00:42:51,413
(tense music)

800
00:42:51,413 --> 00:42:53,743
- [Crow] Paradise sounds
better than this movie.

801
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:56,100
- Still no word from Stingray-

802
00:42:56,100 --> 00:42:57,682
- [Joel] He's got a
remote commode, that guy.

803
00:42:57,682 --> 00:42:58,818
- No, sir.

804
00:42:58,818 --> 00:43:01,524
Oughtn't we to send out search planes?

805
00:43:01,524 --> 00:43:03,534
- We'll give 'em another two hours.

806
00:43:03,534 --> 00:43:06,034
(tense music)

807
00:43:11,640 --> 00:43:14,270
- Well, we made it back okay, Phones.

808
00:43:14,270 --> 00:43:15,640
- Yeah, just in time

809
00:43:16,756 --> 00:43:18,440
