(sonar beeping)

1336
01:06:56,130 --> 01:06:57,470
There goes the depth gauge.

1337
01:06:57,470 --> 01:06:59,680
How much deeper does this tunnel go?

1338
01:06:59,680 --> 01:07:02,340
- This soundings show
we're descending, Troy.

1339
01:07:02,340 --> 01:07:03,173
How about the hull?

1340
01:07:03,173 --> 01:07:06,250
Will it stand the pressure
or will it collapse?

1341
01:07:06,250 --> 01:07:07,260
- I'll let you know.

1342
01:07:12,450 --> 01:07:14,690
- [Joel] Milk's leaking in from outside.

1343
01:07:14,690 --> 01:07:17,543
- That's the hull, and it
doesn't sound very reassuring.

1344
01:07:18,720 --> 01:07:20,890
(glass cracks)

1345
01:07:20,890 --> 01:07:23,120
- Board observation
paneling, it's cracked.

1346
01:07:23,120 --> 01:07:24,470
We've gotta head back, Stingray

1347
01:07:24,470 --> 01:07:25,950
won't take much more of this.

1348
01:07:25,950 --> 01:07:27,660
- Reduce speed, Phones.

1349
01:07:27,660 --> 01:07:29,070
We're going through with this.

1350
01:07:29,070 --> 01:07:31,143
With any luck, she'll hold for a while.

1351
01:07:38,060 --> 01:07:40,050
Look, ahead.

1352
01:07:40,050 --> 01:07:41,030
The end of the tunnel.

1353
01:07:41,030 --> 01:07:43,040
- Yeah, but we're still going down.

1354
01:07:43,040 --> 01:07:45,660
And then the sounding
equipment is failing.

1355
01:07:45,660 --> 01:07:48,013
We're gonna be navigating
blind before long.

1356
01:07:49,070 --> 01:07:50,210
Gee, Troy.

1357
01:07:50,210 --> 01:07:51,050
- [Joel] Just open a window.

1358
01:07:51,050 --> 01:07:52,950
- I can't stand this pressure.

1359
01:07:52,950 --> 01:07:54,810
- No sign of our friend.

1360
01:07:54,810 --> 01:07:55,787
We've lost him.

1361
01:07:59,568 --> 01:08:01,050
Phones.

1362
01:08:01,050 --> 01:08:02,970
This is a subterranean sea.

1363
01:08:02,970 --> 01:08:04,390
An ocean below the Pacific.

1364
01:08:04,390 --> 01:08:05,330
- [Crow] What happened?

1365
01:08:05,330 --> 01:08:06,910
- That accounts for the great depth.

1366
01:08:06,910 --> 01:08:08,880
- [Joel] They're in a subterranean sea.

1367
01:08:08,880 --> 01:08:12,549
- And there's approach
lights on the sea bed.

1368
01:08:12,549 --> 01:08:14,139
(mysterious music)

1369
01:08:14,139 --> 01:08:16,889
(dramatic music)

1370
01:08:22,250 --> 01:08:23,200
- [Joel] More milk.

1371
01:08:23,200 --> 01:08:25,473
Milk's...
- Pretty bad now.

1372
01:08:26,640 --> 01:08:29,310
I can hardly move my arms.

1373
01:08:29,310 --> 01:08:31,050
- [Joel] Why don't they
just open a window?

1374
01:08:31,050 --> 01:08:33,050
- [Phones] It's increasing every minute.

1375
01:08:35,550 --> 01:08:38,133
- If we don't find him soon, Phones,

1376
01:08:39,040 --> 01:08:40,903
we'll have to turn back.

1377
01:08:42,184 --> 01:08:46,362
Stingray won't take much more
of this before she folds up.

1378
01:08:46,362 --> 01:08:48,470
(dramatic music)

1379
01:08:48,470 --> 01:08:49,793
- [Crow] Gypsy says hi.

1380
01:08:49,793 --> 01:08:52,646
- [Joel] Oh, good.

1381
01:08:52,646 --> 01:08:54,790
- [Crow] Another Penzoil enema,
she'll be as good as new.

1382
01:08:54,790 --> 01:08:56,120
- Pretty near.

1383
01:08:56,120 --> 01:08:56,953
- Yeah.

1384
01:08:56,953 --> 01:08:58,310
I can see lights ahead.

1385
01:08:58,310 --> 01:09:00,977
(ominous music)

1386
01:09:05,590 --> 01:09:09,000
- Phones, look at that underwater city.

1387
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:10,500
Must be their base.

1388
01:09:10,500 --> 01:09:12,746
- [Joel] That's no city,
that's a battle station.

1389
01:09:12,746 --> 01:09:15,413
(ominous music)

1390
01:09:17,670 --> 01:09:18,793
Asleep at the wheel.

1391
01:09:23,250 --> 01:09:27,100
- Phones, there's a missile firing craft,

1392
01:09:27,100 --> 01:09:30,510
and it's got us right in its sights.

1393
01:09:30,510 --> 01:09:34,240
We've gotta destroy it, before it gets us.

1394
01:09:34,240 --> 01:09:35,643
I'll need your help.

1395
01:09:36,896 --> 01:09:39,063
- [Crow] Get 'em, get 'em.

1396
01:09:42,381 --> 01:09:45,640
- The Terrainians' craft
has withstood the pressure.

1397
01:09:45,640 --> 01:09:48,984
But from the attitude of the
vessel, their crew haven't.

1398
01:09:48,984 --> 01:09:51,513
(mysterious music)

1399
01:09:51,513 --> 01:09:52,730
- Phones.

1400
01:09:52,730 --> 01:09:53,850
Come on, boy.

1401
01:09:53,850 --> 01:09:54,683
We're in trouble.

1402
01:09:54,683 --> 01:09:56,013
- Now for the kill.

1403
01:09:57,190 --> 01:09:59,023
Launching missile in 10 seconds.

1404
01:10:00,687 --> 01:10:01,777
10.

1405
01:10:01,777 --> 01:10:03,577
- [Joel] Is that 10 marine seconds ?

1406
01:10:06,320 --> 01:10:07,910
Come on, Phones.

1407
01:10:07,910 --> 01:10:11,444
Three, zero, zero, nine.

1408
01:10:11,444 --> 01:10:12,277
Sting one.

1409
01:10:13,366 --> 01:10:16,231
(dramatic music)

1410
01:10:16,231 --> 01:10:17,487
- One.

1411
01:10:17,487 --> 01:10:18,658
Zero.

1412
01:10:18,658 --> 01:10:19,491
(laser blasting)

1413
01:10:19,491 --> 01:10:22,592
(explosion booming)

1414
01:10:22,592 --> 01:10:24,530
- [Joel] You know, maybe he
should get a shorter countdown.

1415
01:10:24,530 --> 01:10:25,853
He keeps getting blasted.

1416
01:10:26,890 --> 01:10:29,290
- [Crow] That's the
problem with undersea life.

1417
01:10:29,290 --> 01:10:30,232
- [Joel] It's those marine seconds.

1418
01:10:30,232 --> 01:10:33,315
(explosions booming)

1419
01:10:34,258 --> 01:10:36,841
(upbeat music)

1420
01:10:55,165 --> 01:10:57,748
(upbeat music)

1421
01:11:05,700 --> 01:11:09,500
- Oh, I must've passed out.

1422
01:11:09,500 --> 01:11:11,913
Say, the cannon's exploded.

1423
01:11:14,580 --> 01:11:18,438
If you can help me, Marina,
we can destroy the city.

1424
01:11:18,438 --> 01:11:19,637
(laser blasting)

1425
01:11:19,637 --> 01:11:21,780
- [Joel] That's your answer
to everything, isn't it?

1426
01:11:21,780 --> 01:11:22,840
Destroy the city.

1427
01:11:22,840 --> 01:11:23,795
- [Crow] Destroy the city.

1428
01:11:23,795 --> 01:11:28,795
(explosion booming)
(dramatic music)

1429
01:11:30,710 --> 01:11:31,590
Joel?

1430
01:11:31,590 --> 01:11:32,720
- [Joel] Yeah?

1431
01:11:32,720 --> 01:11:35,120
- [Crow] Is it possible
for a robot to be bored?

1432
01:11:37,460 --> 01:11:38,760
- [Joel] I don't think so.

1433
01:11:39,997 --> 01:11:41,140
- [Crow] Oh.

1434
01:11:41,140 --> 01:11:42,190
- Okay, Marina.

1435
01:11:42,190 --> 01:11:45,260
Let's get outta here
before Stingray collapses

1436
01:11:45,260 --> 01:11:47,035
like a paper bag.

1437
01:11:47,035 --> 01:11:48,170
(dramatic music)

1438
01:11:48,170 --> 01:11:50,283
- [Joel] You ever
collapsed like a paper bag?

1439
01:11:51,841 --> 01:11:53,340
- [Crow] No.

1440
01:11:53,340 --> 01:11:54,590
- [Joel] It's not pretty.

1441
01:11:55,509 --> 01:11:58,176
- [Crow] I think it wouldn't be.

1442
01:12:00,595 --> 01:12:04,058
(dramatic music)

1443
01:12:04,058 --> 01:12:07,880
- Well, we've learned one
thing out of all this, Tempest.

1444
01:12:07,880 --> 01:12:12,040
Our scientists, designers,
and indeed we ourselves

1445
01:12:12,040 --> 01:12:13,300
are not infallible.

1446
01:12:13,300 --> 01:12:16,090
Marineville's early warning
system needs improving.

1447
01:12:16,090 --> 01:12:18,860
Stingray must be prepared
to go even deeper

1448
01:12:18,860 --> 01:12:20,929
than the deepest ocean.

1449
01:12:20,929 --> 01:12:22,720
- [Crow] I have to drain my radiator

1450
01:12:22,720 --> 01:12:23,553
- [Joel] Okay.

1451
01:12:23,553 --> 01:12:25,890
- Man has never before encountered.

1452
01:12:25,890 --> 01:12:27,990
We've all gotta start working right away

1453
01:12:27,990 --> 01:12:30,540
to equip ourselves for any event.

1454
01:12:30,540 --> 01:12:31,763
- Right, dismissed.

1455
01:12:35,050 --> 01:12:36,320
Okay, Atlanta.

1456
01:12:36,320 --> 01:12:38,008
Let's get started.

1457
01:12:38,008 --> 01:12:38,841
There's no time to lose.

1458
01:12:38,841 --> 01:12:41,440
- [Man On Loudspeaker] Marineville
tracking station calling.

1459
01:12:41,440 --> 01:12:44,040
Remote control undersea survey probe

1460
01:12:44,040 --> 01:12:48,860
in position South-Southwest
200, reference four.

1461
01:12:48,860 --> 01:12:51,450
- Probe signal burying
at 55 and eight-zero

1462
01:12:51,450 --> 01:12:52,763
sonic mega bars coming in.

1463
01:12:54,499 --> 01:12:57,090
- Subload ref gold.

1464
01:12:57,090 --> 01:12:58,750
Start a EG.

1465
01:12:58,750 --> 01:13:00,770
Yes, we'll be through
with this section soon.

1466
01:13:00,770 --> 01:13:02,080
- Yes, Commander.

1467
01:13:02,080 --> 01:13:04,340
This sure is a swell way
to survey the ocean floor.

1468
01:13:04,340 --> 01:13:05,860
- I know it, Lieutenant.

1469
01:13:05,860 --> 01:13:09,380
Kinda like the satellites
that go up to explore space.

1470
01:13:09,380 --> 01:13:11,430
- Yeah, no manpower actually endangered.

1471
01:13:11,430 --> 01:13:13,790
Small team required to
note the probe's findings,

1472
01:13:13,790 --> 01:13:14,623
that's all.

1473
01:13:14,623 --> 01:13:17,567
- Yes, I know another
guy who likes the idea.

1474
01:13:17,567 --> 01:13:19,830
He doesn't have to do any work.

1475
01:13:19,830 --> 01:13:22,343
He can go out and enjoy himself.

1476
01:13:22,343 --> 01:13:25,232
(light jazz music)

1477
01:13:25,232 --> 01:13:26,403
- [Joel] Yeah.

1478
01:13:26,403 --> 01:13:29,736
(Joel snapping fingers)

1479
01:13:32,325 --> 01:13:34,860
- You know, this probe
has me worried, Phones.

1480
01:13:34,860 --> 01:13:36,350
- In what way, Troy?

1481
01:13:36,350 --> 01:13:38,400
- Well, some bright guy could get the idea

1482
01:13:38,400 --> 01:13:40,140
that all undersea vessels should be packed

1483
01:13:40,140 --> 01:13:41,480
with unmanned instruments.

1484
01:13:41,480 --> 01:13:42,700
- Then you'd be out of a job.

1485
01:13:42,700 --> 01:13:44,570
- Yeah, that's what I mean.

1486
01:13:44,570 --> 01:13:47,470
- Gee, Troy, you don't think
it'd to come to that, do ya?

1487
01:13:47,470 --> 01:13:48,690
- Relax, Phones.

1488
01:13:48,690 --> 01:13:50,170
I was only kiddin'.

1489
01:13:50,170 --> 01:13:51,700
- All the same, just thick.

1490
01:13:51,700 --> 01:13:54,510
Here we are, nice and snug while sea probe

1491
01:13:54,510 --> 01:13:58,224
is in that cold old sea
doing all the work for us.

1492
01:13:58,224 --> 01:14:01,064
(dramatic music)

1493
01:14:01,064 --> 01:14:03,731
(sonar beeping)

1494
01:14:05,850 --> 01:14:07,400
- [Joel] Sounds like
there's a cuckoo clock

1495
01:14:07,400 --> 01:14:09,371
on that sea probe.

1496
01:14:09,371 --> 01:14:14,371
(sonar beeping)
(mysterious music)

1497
01:14:25,880 --> 01:14:27,453
Drives fish crazy.

1498
01:14:32,412 --> 01:14:33,858
(dramatic music)

1499
01:14:33,858 --> 01:14:35,120
- [Commander] What's
happening, Lieutenant?

1500
01:14:35,120 --> 01:14:36,280
The signal's fading.

1501
01:14:36,280 --> 01:14:38,420
- The probe seems to have gone
beneath the ocean bed, sir.

1502
01:14:38,420 --> 01:14:41,110
- What do you mean beneath the ocean bed?

1503
01:14:41,110 --> 01:14:43,493
There are no fissures
or cracks in that area.

1504
01:14:48,120 --> 01:14:52,235
Wait, there's a submerged
extinct volcano there,

1505
01:14:52,235 --> 01:14:54,210
and the crater appears to be enormous.

1506
01:14:54,210 --> 01:14:55,400
- Yeah.

1507
01:14:55,400 --> 01:14:56,430
A Magnum.

1508
01:14:56,430 --> 01:14:59,000
The biggest bottle of
champagne they've got.

1509
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:00,450
I ordered it when we came in.

1510
01:15:00,450 --> 01:15:03,340
- Aww, gee, Troy, you sure
are living it up tonight.

1511
01:15:03,340 --> 01:15:04,590
- And why not?

1512
01:15:04,590 --> 01:15:06,019
We deserve it just this once, I guess.

1513
01:15:06,019 --> 01:15:07,453
- Hey Crow.
- Hey Joel Hodgson.

1514
01:15:08,290 --> 01:15:09,233
What did I miss?

1515
01:15:10,084 --> 01:15:11,310
- [Joel] Nothing, the same thing,

1516
01:15:11,310 --> 01:15:13,030
they destroyed the underwater city

1517
01:15:13,030 --> 01:15:15,836
and now we're back at Marineville.

1518
01:15:15,836 --> 01:15:18,110
- [Crow] What's the tally now?

1519
01:15:18,110 --> 01:15:20,860
- [Joel] Three alien
civilizations have been wiped out.

1520
01:15:22,455 --> 01:15:23,345
- [Crow] That's a good day.

1521
01:15:23,345 --> 01:15:24,900
- That's the tower.

1522
01:15:24,900 --> 01:15:26,093
Hold the champagne.

1523
01:15:27,230 --> 01:15:28,329
What's wrong, Commander?

1524
01:15:28,329 --> 01:15:29,677
- [Commander] Plenty.

1525
01:15:29,677 --> 01:15:32,610
- [Joel] These guys never get a break.

1526
01:15:32,610 --> 01:15:34,520
- I want you to report
to the tower immediately

1527
01:15:34,520 --> 01:15:37,340
so that I can fill you
in with all the details.

1528
01:15:37,340 --> 01:15:40,007
And I want Stingray to carry
out a full investigation.

1529
01:15:40,007 --> 01:15:42,507
(tense music)

1530
01:15:48,660 --> 01:15:52,040
- [Joel] Sounds like it's
time to lower the city again.

1531
01:15:52,040 --> 01:15:54,074
- [Crow] It's the Conga music.

1532
01:15:54,074 --> 01:15:56,824
(dramatic music)

1533
01:15:59,460 --> 01:16:01,330
It's nice that they've
made the transformation

1534
01:16:01,330 --> 01:16:03,430
from standard alarms to Conga music.

1535
01:16:03,430 --> 01:16:04,759
- Stingray seaborne.

1536
01:16:04,759 --> 01:16:05,793
- Okay, Troy.

1537
01:16:05,793 --> 01:16:08,630
Proceed to position
South-Southwest 2000 reference-

1538
01:16:08,630 --> 01:16:10,020
- [Joel] He's talking
into one of those things

1539
01:16:10,020 --> 01:16:11,960
you examine your ears with.

1540
01:16:11,960 --> 01:16:13,170
- [Commander] You'd better
wear the high frequency

1541
01:16:13,170 --> 01:16:15,296
tracking pack in case you're
pulled down to the volcano

1542
01:16:15,296 --> 01:16:16,380
like the probe.

1543
01:16:16,380 --> 01:16:17,480
- Yes, sir.

1544
01:16:17,480 --> 01:16:19,310
That'll keep us in signal
contact up to a depth

1545
01:16:19,310 --> 01:16:20,815
of four miles from the ocean bed.

1546
01:16:20,815 --> 01:16:22,230
- Four miles?

1547
01:16:22,230 --> 01:16:24,820
No extinct volcano can be that deep.

1548
01:16:24,820 --> 01:16:26,680
- We've come up against
stranger things than that

1549
01:16:26,680 --> 01:16:27,513
beneath the sea.

1550
01:16:27,513 --> 01:16:28,480
- [Crow] I didn't need no...

1551
01:16:29,410 --> 01:16:30,243
Nevermind.

1552
01:16:30,243 --> 01:16:31,080
- Rate six.

1553
01:16:31,080 --> 01:16:33,580
(tense music)

1554
01:16:51,920 --> 01:16:54,370
- Stingray in area reference four, sir.

1555
01:16:54,370 --> 01:16:55,203
- Okay, Atlanta.

1556
01:16:55,203 --> 01:16:56,852
Keep a close track.

1557
01:16:56,852 --> 01:16:57,685
If anything is gonna happen, it'll be

1558
01:16:57,685 --> 01:16:59,507
within the next few seconds.

1559
01:16:59,507 --> 01:17:03,120
(suspenseful music)

1560
01:17:03,120 --> 01:17:04,540
- Crater dead ahead.

1561
01:17:04,540 --> 01:17:06,150
- This is where the trouble started.

1562
01:17:06,150 --> 01:17:07,505
Stand by, Phones.

1563
01:17:07,505 --> 01:17:10,505
(suspenseful music)

1564
01:17:16,863 --> 01:17:21,326
- [Crow] They're lucky to
find an extinct volcano.

1565
01:17:21,326 --> 01:17:23,326
I didn't even know they were endangered.

1566
01:17:28,310 --> 01:17:29,660
- Hey, we're going down!

1567
01:17:29,660 --> 01:17:30,860
We're being pulled down!

1568
01:17:30,860 --> 01:17:31,810
- Blow three and seven.

1569
01:17:31,810 --> 01:17:33,480
We've gotta keep her on an even keel.

1570
01:17:33,480 --> 01:17:34,680
- [Joel] Pull my finger.

1571
01:17:36,690 --> 01:17:38,090
- Marineville from Stingray.

1572
01:17:38,090 --> 01:17:40,880
We're being pulled into the volcano.

1573
01:17:40,880 --> 01:17:42,480
- [Commander] Stingray from tower.

1574
01:17:42,480 --> 01:17:44,649
I didn't get your last message.

1575
01:17:44,649 --> 01:17:47,410
Please repeat last message.

1576
01:17:47,410 --> 01:17:49,730
- Start high-frequency
tracking pack, Phones.

1577
01:17:49,730 --> 01:17:51,203
Normal radio contact fading.

1578
01:17:57,770 --> 01:17:59,100
- The tracking pack's operating.

1579
01:17:59,100 --> 01:17:59,933
- Yeah.

1580
01:17:59,933 --> 01:18:01,840
They're going beneath the ocean bed.

1581
01:18:01,840 --> 01:18:03,310
Tap in again, Atlanta.

1582
01:18:03,310 --> 01:18:07,262
Cypher signal is our only contact
with Stingray from now on.

1583
01:18:07,262 --> 01:18:10,179
(mysterious music)

1584
01:18:14,760 --> 01:18:17,293
- We're a thousand feet
beneath the ocean bed.

1585
01:18:18,130 --> 01:18:19,490
- Operate sounding echo.

1586
01:18:19,490 --> 01:18:21,440
I want to know how deep this crater is.

1587
01:18:23,450 --> 01:18:25,950
(tense music)

1588
01:18:29,130 --> 01:18:30,913
- [Crow] Oh, it's much deeper than that.

1589
01:18:33,124 --> 01:18:34,291
- [Joel] Echo.

1590
01:18:37,811 --> 01:18:40,394
(gentle music)

1591
01:18:42,599 --> 01:18:44,927
(dramatic music)

1592
01:18:44,927 --> 01:18:47,242
(sonar beeping)

1593
01:18:47,242 --> 01:18:48,617
- Jumpin' catfish.

1594
01:18:48,617 --> 01:18:51,090
I thought we'd never get that echo.

1595
01:18:51,090 --> 01:18:52,990
- Two and a half miles, Troy.

1596
01:18:52,990 --> 01:18:55,050
That's the crater's depth.

1597
01:18:55,050 --> 01:18:56,347
- Now we want to find
out what's waiting for us

1598
01:18:56,347 --> 01:18:57,433
at the bottom.

1599
01:18:58,580 --> 01:19:00,060
- [Crow] Why are they
monitoring their heart rate

1600
01:19:00,060 --> 01:19:01,100
at such a low depth

1601
01:19:05,010 --> 01:19:06,950
- Tracking signal half strike.

1602
01:19:06,950 --> 01:19:10,331
- That's two miles beneath the sea bed.

1603
01:19:10,331 --> 01:19:11,970
Thank heavens we know Stingray can stand

1604
01:19:11,970 --> 01:19:12,970
that water pressure.

1605
01:19:16,380 --> 01:19:18,870
- Less than 2000 feet to bottom, Troy.

1606
01:19:18,870 --> 01:19:21,600
- Nearly two and a half miles.

1607
01:19:21,600 --> 01:19:23,690
And they're still increasing depth rate.

1608
01:19:23,690 --> 01:19:25,990
- Why doesn't Troy slow her up?

1609
01:19:25,990 --> 01:19:27,540
Blow tanks, Troy, now.

1610
01:19:28,730 --> 01:19:30,159
- Blow all tanks.

1611
01:19:30,159 --> 01:19:30,992
Now.

1612
01:19:30,992 --> 01:19:33,742
(dramatic music)

1613
01:19:34,967 --> 01:19:36,900
- We're going faster.
- How much further?

1614
01:19:36,900 --> 01:19:38,470
- 200 feet.

1615
01:19:38,470 --> 01:19:39,315
This is it.

1616
01:19:39,315 --> 01:19:42,440
(mysterious music)

1617
01:19:42,440 --> 01:19:45,133
- We're slowing down.
- 20 feet to go.

1618
01:19:51,990 --> 01:19:53,960
- [Crow] That's very well
for the bottom of a crater

1619
01:19:53,960 --> 01:19:56,882
of an abandoned volcano
in the bottom of the sea.

1620
01:19:56,882 --> 01:19:58,750
- [Joel] I was just gonna say that.

1621
01:19:58,750 --> 01:20:00,363
- [Crow] I beat you this time.

1622
01:20:03,610 --> 01:20:04,773
- What is this place?

1623
01:20:05,890 --> 01:20:08,853
- I can't say, Troy,
it's difficult to see.

1624
01:20:10,964 --> 01:20:13,631
(ominous music)

1625
01:20:16,675 --> 01:20:19,675
(suspenseful music)

1626
01:20:22,845 --> 01:20:24,400
- Phones.

1627
01:20:24,400 --> 01:20:27,063
Look, there's some kinda door over there.

1628
01:20:28,101 --> 01:20:29,573
- [Man] Attention, Terranians.

1629
01:20:30,780 --> 01:20:31,963
Listen carefully.

1630
01:20:33,060 --> 01:20:37,580
You will swim out of your
craft towards the door.

1631
01:20:37,580 --> 01:20:39,253
It is an airlock.

1632
01:20:39,253 --> 01:20:40,993
- Where's that voice coming from?

1633
01:20:41,940 --> 01:20:43,629
- It's all around us, Troy.

1634
01:20:43,629 --> 01:20:46,190
- [Man] Approach the airlock.

1635
01:20:46,190 --> 01:20:47,310
- What do we do?

1636
01:20:47,310 --> 01:20:49,480
- My first thought is to
hightail it outta here.

1637
01:20:49,480 --> 01:20:53,880
- [Man] Obey me, or it
will be disastrous for you.

1638
01:20:53,880 --> 01:20:55,082
- What does it mean?

1639
01:20:55,082 --> 01:20:56,259
- That, I guess.

1640
01:20:56,259 --> 01:20:58,759
(tense music)

1641
01:21:03,966 --> 01:21:06,610
- [Crow] That would be
disastrous all right.

1642
01:21:06,610 --> 01:21:08,250
- The tracking signal's been constant

1643
01:21:08,250 --> 01:21:09,950
for 15 minutes, Father.

1644
01:21:09,950 --> 01:21:10,970
- Yeah.

1645
01:21:10,970 --> 01:21:13,600
Registering a depth of
two and one half miles

1646
01:21:13,600 --> 01:21:14,670
beneath the ocean.

1647
01:21:14,670 --> 01:21:16,790
- Well, what could have happened?

1648
01:21:16,790 --> 01:21:18,823
Why doesn't the signal change?

1649
01:21:20,403 --> 01:21:22,650
- [Joel] Maybe they're ignoring her.

1650
01:21:22,650 --> 01:21:23,750
- [Crow] I sure would.

1651
01:21:51,890 --> 01:21:54,900
- Obey the rules or we'll
give you a penicillin shot.

1652
01:21:54,900 --> 01:21:58,867
Right where it counts.
(Joel chuckles)

1653
01:22:02,946 --> 01:22:05,446
(tense music)

1654
01:22:07,490 --> 01:22:10,240
(water bubbling)

1655
01:22:16,972 --> 01:22:18,336
- Where do we go from here?

1656
01:22:18,336 --> 01:22:19,390
- Yeah.

1657
01:22:19,390 --> 01:22:20,593
There's no other door.

1658
01:22:21,690 --> 01:22:25,196
- [Man] Now, operate the control.

1659
01:22:25,196 --> 01:22:27,990
- Man said "Operate the control."

1660
01:22:27,990 --> 01:22:28,823
This must be it.

1661
01:22:32,678 --> 01:22:33,511
- We're going down.

1662
01:22:33,511 --> 01:22:35,123
- Yeah, and what a pace.

1663
01:22:37,438 --> 01:22:40,423
(signal beeping)

1664
01:22:40,423 --> 01:22:43,740
- We can be pretty sure
they're still okay, Atlanta.

1665
01:22:43,740 --> 01:22:46,740
- Yes, father, but they're
going deeper, and so swiftly.

1666
01:22:46,740 --> 01:22:48,457
It's almost as if they're heading

1667
01:22:48,457 --> 01:22:50,139
for the center of the Earth.

1668
01:22:50,139 --> 01:22:52,806
(ominous music)

1669
01:22:55,580 --> 01:22:56,590
- How deep are we, Phones?

1670
01:22:56,590 --> 01:22:57,883
- I don't know.

1671
01:22:58,863 --> 01:23:01,497
We must be about four miles
beneath the ocean bed, Troy.

1672
01:23:01,497 --> 01:23:03,621
- And we're on our own.

1673
01:23:03,621 --> 01:23:05,604
Marineville will have
lost all track of us.

1674
01:23:05,604 --> 01:23:08,271
(signal fading)

1675
01:23:09,780 --> 01:23:11,550
- It's gone, Father.

1676
01:23:11,550 --> 01:23:13,302
We've lost contact.

1677
01:23:13,302 --> 01:23:15,007
- Yeah.

1678
01:23:15,007 --> 01:23:17,040
They're beyond the transmitter's range.

1679
01:23:17,040 --> 01:23:18,987
Over four miles beneath the sea bed.

1680
01:23:22,338 --> 01:23:25,421
(explosions booming)

1681
01:23:26,457 --> 01:23:29,040
(upbeat music)

1682
01:23:50,438 --> 01:23:53,021
(upbeat music)

1683
01:23:56,016 --> 01:23:57,078
(Gypsy groaning)

1684
01:23:57,078 --> 01:23:58,203
- People of Earth.

1685
01:23:58,203 --> 01:24:01,320
As you can see, some alien form of disease

1686
01:24:01,320 --> 01:24:04,430
has infected my satellite and affected

1687
01:24:04,430 --> 01:24:07,200
all the robots and
carbon-based life forms.

1688
01:24:07,200 --> 01:24:08,730
- How's he doing, Joel Hodgson?

1689
01:24:08,730 --> 01:24:10,520
- Well, it's kinda hard to tell, Crow,

1690
01:24:10,520 --> 01:24:14,020
with this weird snake
thermometer I've got.

1691
01:24:14,020 --> 01:24:15,570
- This might be a bad time to bring it up,

1692
01:24:15,570 --> 01:24:18,398
Joel Hodgson, but wouldn't that make it

1693
01:24:18,398 --> 01:24:19,540
a rectal thermometer?

1694
01:24:19,540 --> 01:24:21,149
- Yuck.
- Ew.

1695
01:24:21,149 --> 01:24:24,221
(Gypsy shrieking)

1696
01:24:24,221 --> 01:24:25,271
- Oh, jeez.
- Uh-oh.

1697
01:24:26,950 --> 01:24:29,060
- Crow, we gotta find
out what this stuff is

1698
01:24:29,060 --> 01:24:31,640
before it gets serious, ugh.

1699
01:24:31,640 --> 01:24:33,210
- I don't know what it
is, but it's certainly

1700
01:24:33,210 --> 01:24:34,690
not one of the four food groups.

1701
01:24:34,690 --> 01:24:35,830
- That's for sure.

1702
01:24:35,830 --> 01:24:39,990
It's affected the robots, the
plant life, everything but...

1703
01:24:42,460 --> 01:24:43,577
- Humans?

1704
01:24:43,577 --> 01:24:46,244
(Joel sneezing)

1705
01:24:48,500 --> 01:24:50,570
- Oh, Crow, we got movie sign.

1706
01:24:50,570 --> 01:24:51,810
We gotta get outta here.

1707
01:24:51,810 --> 01:24:52,754
Let's go.

1708
01:24:52,754 --> 01:24:54,035
(alarm buzzes)

1709
01:24:54,035 --> 01:24:56,702
(doors opening)

1710
01:25:04,465 --> 01:25:05,992
- We're slowing up.

1711
01:25:05,992 --> 01:25:08,492
(tense music)

1712
01:25:18,401 --> 01:25:22,188
- [Man] Welcome to Voldana, Terrainians.

1713
01:25:22,188 --> 01:25:26,324
- [Joel] I don't know what
happened, I just sat down.

1714
01:25:26,324 --> 01:25:28,657
- [Crow] Okay, Joel Hodgson.

1715
01:25:30,090 --> 01:25:31,500
- [Joel] Isn't that Memphis furniture?

1716
01:25:31,500 --> 01:25:34,110
- You have arrived just in time.

1717
01:25:34,110 --> 01:25:34,943
- Who are you?

1718
01:25:34,943 --> 01:25:36,240
- Memphis?
- What is this place?

1719
01:25:36,240 --> 01:25:38,370
- My name is Turata.

1720
01:25:38,370 --> 01:25:40,420
This is Fragil.

1721
01:25:40,420 --> 01:25:44,440
We are the sole survivors of Zentralius,

1722
01:25:44,440 --> 01:25:47,860
the mighty civilization that
has lived under the Earth

1723
01:25:47,860 --> 01:25:49,900
for thousands of years.

1724
01:25:49,900 --> 01:25:54,233
- Alas, this room is the only
part of our dynamic city left,

1725
01:25:54,233 --> 01:25:56,590
for a great disaster struck.

1726
01:25:56,590 --> 01:25:59,238
- You mean every one
of your people is dead?

1727
01:25:59,238 --> 01:26:00,655
- Yes, Terranian.

1728
01:26:01,670 --> 01:26:02,860
- [Crow] Not everyone.

1729
01:26:02,860 --> 01:26:05,135
- When the volcano, became active.

1730
01:26:05,135 --> 01:26:06,650
I will explain.

1731
01:26:06,650 --> 01:26:08,497
(ominous music)

1732
01:26:08,497 --> 01:26:10,397
- [Joel] Oh, that' chart's real handy.

1733
01:26:11,236 --> 01:26:14,729
- Built within the shaft
of the dormant volcano.

1734
01:26:14,729 --> 01:26:17,849
We were luckily-
- Central control.

1735
01:26:17,849 --> 01:26:19,483
And Volandria's right there.

1736
01:26:19,483 --> 01:26:20,900
- Destroyed by the lava, huh?

1737
01:26:20,900 --> 01:26:21,920
- [Turata] Yes.

1738
01:26:21,920 --> 01:26:25,553
We managed to secure and
seal the protecting door.

1739
01:26:30,530 --> 01:26:31,743
- What happened then?

1740
01:26:31,743 --> 01:26:35,290
- The activity subsided and we were safe.

1741
01:26:35,290 --> 01:26:36,343
- Until now.

1742
01:26:37,250 --> 01:26:39,260
If you listen carefully, you can hear

1743
01:26:39,260 --> 01:26:43,623
the fury of the volcano,
just beyond these very walls.

1744
01:26:43,623 --> 01:26:44,750
(tense music)

1745
01:26:44,750 --> 01:26:45,780
- [Crow] That's what happens when you make

1746
01:26:45,780 --> 01:26:48,690
a seal of protection.
(Joel chuckles)

1747
01:26:48,690 --> 01:26:51,828
- Soon the volcano will erupt again.

1748
01:26:51,828 --> 01:26:54,823
Then our last refuge will be destroyed.

1749
01:26:54,823 --> 01:26:58,650
- That is why we used our
electronic suction apparatus

1750
01:26:58,650 --> 01:27:00,600
to draw in the first crack.

1751
01:27:00,600 --> 01:27:02,270
- You mean a vacuum.
- I don't understand.

1752
01:27:02,270 --> 01:27:05,370
- Like you, we cannot breathe in water.

1753
01:27:05,370 --> 01:27:08,100
We needed the crack to reach the terrain.

1754
01:27:08,100 --> 01:27:13,100
- But alas, the craft we
chose was full of instruments.

1755
01:27:13,120 --> 01:27:14,970
There was no room for us.

1756
01:27:14,970 --> 01:27:16,850
- So you drew Stingray down, eh?

1757
01:27:16,850 --> 01:27:19,692
- But why all the threats
with the missiles?

1758
01:27:19,692 --> 01:27:21,285
That wasn't very friendly.

1759
01:27:21,285 --> 01:27:22,260
- [Crow] It was full of instruments?

1760
01:27:22,260 --> 01:27:25,770
Music is important, but isn't life good?

1761
01:27:25,770 --> 01:27:27,743
- [Joel] It was filled
with the marine gold.

1762
01:27:29,225 --> 01:27:31,750
(volcano rumbling)

1763
01:27:31,750 --> 01:27:34,350
- Sounds like the volcano's ready to blow.

1764
01:27:34,350 --> 01:27:35,700
We better get outta here.

1765
01:27:35,700 --> 01:27:39,430
- Yes, but how do we get to
your ship from the airlock?

1766
01:27:39,430 --> 01:27:40,570
- Stingray's hatches open.

1767
01:27:40,570 --> 01:27:42,710
We can swim straight in.

1768
01:27:42,710 --> 01:27:43,770
There's only one problem.

1769
01:27:43,770 --> 01:27:45,695
- [Crow] It's full of water.

1770
01:27:45,695 --> 01:27:47,850
- Only got two sets of breathing gear.

1771
01:27:47,850 --> 01:27:51,153
- In that case, there is no problem.

1772
01:27:52,120 --> 01:27:55,231
We will take the breathing apparatus.

1773
01:27:55,231 --> 01:27:57,920
- You dirty rats.
- The guns.

1774
01:27:57,920 --> 01:27:59,630
- [Joel] Water rats.

1775
01:27:59,630 --> 01:28:00,590
- But the volcano-

1776
01:28:00,590 --> 01:28:02,757
- One more second and you die now!

1777
01:28:02,757 --> 01:28:05,080
- He means it, Phones.

1778
01:28:05,080 --> 01:28:06,750
Maybe there's some other
way out of this mess.

1779
01:28:06,750 --> 01:28:07,633
Do as he says.

1780
01:28:08,710 --> 01:28:10,395
- [Crow] No, that's not it.

1781
01:28:10,395 --> 01:28:13,062
(Joel chuckles)

1782
01:28:16,703 --> 01:28:19,440
- Come, Fragil, we must be leaving.

1783
01:28:26,623 --> 01:28:30,290
We would not want to
prolong your suffering.

1784
01:28:31,166 --> 01:28:33,174
We are humane people.

1785
01:28:33,174 --> 01:28:34,179
(suspenseful music)

1786
01:28:34,179 --> 01:28:35,163
(gunshot bangs)

1787
01:28:35,163 --> 01:28:36,833
(explosion booming)

1788
01:28:36,833 --> 01:28:39,040
- [Crow] Don't you have
to be human to be humane?

1789
01:28:39,040 --> 01:28:40,498
- [Joel] Yeah.

1790
01:28:40,498 --> 01:28:44,415
Looks like they're gonna
have a puppet hibachi.

1791
01:28:46,712 --> 01:28:49,379
(Crow chuckles)

1792
01:28:54,010 --> 01:28:56,183
- [Crow] Goodness gracious.

1793
01:28:56,183 --> 01:28:58,433
- And the lava's spreading.

1794
01:29:01,050 --> 01:29:04,030
- [Joel] Wouldn't be
lava if it didn't spread.

1795
01:29:04,030 --> 01:29:05,700
- There's only one hope.
- It'd be a rock.

1796
01:29:05,700 --> 01:29:06,857
- Marina.

1797
01:29:06,857 --> 01:29:09,440
(solemn music)

1798
01:29:12,240 --> 01:29:14,433
- [Crow] Their hair will rust.

1799
01:29:14,433 --> 01:29:17,100
(Joel chuckles)

1800
01:29:19,200 --> 01:29:20,700
- [Joel] Honk the horn at 'em.

1801
01:29:23,576 --> 01:29:26,967
- [Crow] Maybe if she flashes
the brights, they'll go away.

1802
01:29:35,328 --> 01:29:36,813
- [Turata] What do we do now?

1803
01:29:36,813 --> 01:29:40,770
The hatch is closed, we cannot get in.

1804
01:29:40,770 --> 01:29:42,393
- [Joel] Take off your swim gear.

1805
01:29:43,730 --> 01:29:45,883
- [Crow] Will that make
them easier to get in?

1806
01:29:46,840 --> 01:29:47,673
- [Joel] No.

1807
01:29:49,120 --> 01:29:50,453
So it wasn't that funny.

1808
01:29:51,912 --> 01:29:54,000
(Crow laughing)

1809
01:29:54,000 --> 01:29:54,833
Thank you.

1810
01:29:56,307 --> 01:29:58,960
- The Terrainians have
played a little trick on us.

1811
01:29:58,960 --> 01:30:00,800
Now it is our turn.

1812
01:30:00,800 --> 01:30:02,261
We will get them up here-

1813
01:30:02,261 --> 01:30:03,250
- [Crow] It would
probably make that problem

1814
01:30:03,250 --> 01:30:04,945
seem less important, though.

1815
01:30:04,945 --> 01:30:07,945
(suspenseful music)

1816
01:30:18,890 --> 01:30:22,218
They could wait for it to
harden and sell it as soap.

1817
01:30:22,218 --> 01:30:23,051
(Joel chuckles)

1818
01:30:23,051 --> 01:30:24,383
- The whole place is gonna collapse.

1819
01:30:24,383 --> 01:30:27,383
(suspenseful music)

1820
01:30:32,370 --> 01:30:34,960
- We must act swiftly if we are to escape.

1821
01:30:34,960 --> 01:30:37,610
- The Terranianians will give no trouble.

1822
01:30:37,610 --> 01:30:41,540
They are unarmed, remember,
and they are experienced enough

1823
01:30:41,540 --> 01:30:45,663
to manage without breathing
gear until we reach the hatch.

1824
01:30:45,663 --> 01:30:47,483
(suspenseful music)

1825
01:30:47,483 --> 01:30:49,894
- [Crow] Because that's
the kind of guys they are.

1826
01:30:49,894 --> 01:30:51,227
- [Joel] Humane.

1827
01:30:53,080 --> 01:30:54,413
- [Crow] Pardon.

1828
01:30:56,703 --> 01:30:57,536
- Phones.

1829
01:30:58,440 --> 01:31:00,520
The elevator's coming down.

1830
01:31:00,520 --> 01:31:01,610
They must be returning.

1831
01:31:01,610 --> 01:31:04,110
(tense music)

1832
01:31:06,618 --> 01:31:09,618
(suspenseful music)

1833
01:31:19,640 --> 01:31:21,093
- [Crow] Wow, baked beans.

1834
01:31:22,099 --> 01:31:23,513
- I do not see them.

1835
01:31:24,773 --> 01:31:26,960
Ah, they must have collapsed.

1836
01:31:26,960 --> 01:31:28,940
(dramatic music)

1837
01:31:28,940 --> 01:31:31,330
- [Joel] No, he must've collapsed.

1838
01:31:31,330 --> 01:31:34,203
- We're not finished yet,
but I guess you two are.

1839
01:31:34,203 --> 01:31:36,010
Get 'em into the elevator, Phones, hurry.

1840
01:31:36,010 --> 01:31:37,240
- [Joel] And remember, all these puppets

1841
01:31:37,240 --> 01:31:39,680
are doing their own stunts, Crow.

1842
01:31:39,680 --> 01:31:42,210
- [Crow] That's important
when you're a puppet.

1843
01:31:42,210 --> 01:31:44,400
- [Joel] At what point does
a puppet quit being a puppet

1844
01:31:44,400 --> 01:31:46,040
and become a costume, Crow?

1845
01:31:46,040 --> 01:31:48,540
(tense music)

1846
01:31:50,523 --> 01:31:53,606
- [Crow] When he pays his union dues.

1847
01:31:54,810 --> 01:31:56,010
- [Joel] Good one.

1848
01:31:56,010 --> 01:31:58,413
- [Crow] Thank you. (chuckles)

1849
01:32:14,489 --> 01:32:16,310
