Their ears aren't even bleeding.

1866
01:33:10,543 --> 01:33:13,210
(Joel chuckles)

1867
01:33:15,890 --> 01:33:18,973
(explosions booming)

1868
01:33:22,490 --> 01:33:25,171
That's what it is to be a good aquanaut.

1869
01:33:25,171 --> 01:33:28,171
(suspenseful music)

1870
01:33:37,272 --> 01:33:40,355
(explosions booming)

1871
01:33:41,381 --> 01:33:43,105
♪ Smoke under water ♪

1872
01:33:43,105 --> 01:33:44,225
(Joel chuckles)

1873
01:33:44,225 --> 01:33:47,949
♪ Fire in the sky ♪

1874
01:33:47,949 --> 01:33:50,874
♪ Smoke under water ♪

1875
01:33:50,874 --> 01:33:53,874
(suspenseful music)

1876
01:34:04,263 --> 01:34:06,020
- Nearly there, Troy.

1877
01:34:06,020 --> 01:34:07,840
- When we hit the ocean,
dive to the seabed.

1878
01:34:07,840 --> 01:34:09,010
You want to be out of the line of fire

1879
01:34:09,010 --> 01:34:10,118
when the volcano blows.

1880
01:34:10,118 --> 01:34:12,618
(tense music)

1881
01:34:14,390 --> 01:34:15,223
- [Crow] What about the submarine

1882
01:34:15,223 --> 01:34:16,773
with the soundtrack musicians?

1883
01:34:18,639 --> 01:34:22,380
(suspenseful music)

1884
01:34:22,380 --> 01:34:23,930
They're always the first to go.

1885
01:34:30,336 --> 01:34:33,419
(explosions booming)

1886
01:34:41,150 --> 01:34:42,529
- Tower to Stingray.

1887
01:34:42,529 --> 01:34:43,612
Are you okay?

1888
01:34:45,889 --> 01:34:47,903
Come in, Stingray.

1889
01:34:47,903 --> 01:34:49,340
Troy!

1890
01:34:49,340 --> 01:34:50,173
Speak to me.

1891
01:34:52,690 --> 01:34:53,750
- Hang on, Phones.

1892
01:34:53,750 --> 01:34:55,600
We've gotta ride out this tidal wave.

1893
01:35:03,980 --> 01:35:05,583
- [Crow] Now that's hanging 10.

1894
01:35:10,370 --> 01:35:12,520
- Stingray from tower.

1895
01:35:12,520 --> 01:35:13,353
Are you okay?

1896
01:35:16,500 --> 01:35:17,333
Answer me, Troy.

1897
01:35:18,240 --> 01:35:19,073
Troy!

1898
01:35:20,160 --> 01:35:21,630
Come in, Stingray.

1899
01:35:21,630 --> 01:35:23,270
This is Atlanta.

1900
01:35:23,270 --> 01:35:24,453
Are you okay?

1901
01:35:27,440 --> 01:35:28,823
- Tower from Stingray.

1902
01:35:30,530 --> 01:35:31,613
We're okay, Atlanta.

1903
01:35:32,460 --> 01:35:33,563
- Oh, Troy.

1904
01:35:34,570 --> 01:35:35,713
You're safe.

1905
01:35:36,770 --> 01:35:37,840
You're safe.

1906
01:35:37,840 --> 01:35:39,087
- Yeah, we're safe.

1907
01:35:39,087 --> 01:35:41,740
And we've got a couple of passengers, too.

1908
01:35:41,740 --> 01:35:43,690
Tell the commander to
have the cooler ready.

1909
01:35:43,690 --> 01:35:45,303
These are real unpleasant guys.

1910
01:35:46,200 --> 01:35:49,720
Oh, and tell Luigi to have
the champagne standing by.

1911
01:35:49,720 --> 01:35:51,093
I guess we've earned it.

1912
01:35:51,093 --> 01:35:52,260
(light jazz music)

1913
01:35:52,260 --> 01:35:55,280
- [Joel] Think the lab
boys will cut 'em open?

1914
01:35:55,280 --> 01:35:56,518
- [Crow] We can only hope.

1915
01:35:56,518 --> 01:35:59,950
(light jazz music)

1916
01:35:59,950 --> 01:36:01,770
- [Joel] Looks like Red Skelton on bass,

1917
01:36:01,770 --> 01:36:04,370
Sid Caesar on drums and
Elvis Costello at the piano.

1918
01:36:06,380 --> 01:36:07,620
- [Crow] What a combo.

1919
01:36:07,620 --> 01:36:09,659
Swing it.
This is where we came in.

1920
01:36:09,659 --> 01:36:12,916
(Atlanta chuckles)

1921
01:36:12,916 --> 01:36:15,458
(Joel and Crow chuckling)

1922
01:36:15,458 --> 01:36:16,429
- [Joel] Oh boy.

1923
01:36:16,429 --> 01:36:19,960
(explosions booming)

1924
01:36:19,960 --> 01:36:22,543
(upbeat music)

1925
01:36:40,685 --> 01:36:43,268
(upbeat music)

1926
01:36:45,706 --> 01:36:48,531
(tense music)

1927
01:36:48,531 --> 01:36:49,790
Well, that's the end of the show.

1928
01:36:49,790 --> 01:36:51,300
Hey, stay tuned back there.

1929
01:36:51,300 --> 01:36:55,430
When we get back to the
main part of the show.

1930
01:36:55,430 --> 01:36:57,296
- [Crow] We could review
the show, Joel Hodgson.

1931
01:36:57,296 --> 01:36:58,860
- [Joel] Yeah, we could
be Siskel and Ebert.

1932
01:36:58,860 --> 01:37:00,728
- [Crow] I'll be the fat
guy, you be the bald guy.

1933
01:37:00,728 --> 01:37:01,561
- [Joel] Okay.

1934
01:37:01,561 --> 01:37:02,394
Well, what did you think?

1935
01:37:02,394 --> 01:37:04,460
- [Crow] Well, I thought
it was long, boring,

1936
01:37:04,460 --> 01:37:07,540
kinda tedious and stupid, but
I have to give it a claws-up

1937
01:37:07,540 --> 01:37:09,480
because I kinda sympathize
with the puppets.

1938
01:37:09,480 --> 01:37:11,100
- [Joel] Yeah. (chuckles)

1939
01:37:11,100 --> 01:37:13,700
Yeah, what really always baffled me

1940
01:37:13,700 --> 01:37:16,240
is how they could keep those puppets

1941
01:37:16,240 --> 01:37:18,640
from floating to the surface
all the time, you know?

1942
01:37:18,640 --> 01:37:20,310
- [Crow] It's amazing, though.

1943
01:37:20,310 --> 01:37:21,717
I will have to give a definite thumbs-up

1944
01:37:21,717 --> 01:37:23,300
for the special effects used.

1945
01:37:23,300 --> 01:37:24,670
- [Joel] Yeah, I definitely think so.

1946
01:37:24,670 --> 01:37:26,890
And how they got that
fire to go on underwater?

1947
01:37:26,890 --> 01:37:28,070
- [Crow] Smoke in the water.

1948
01:37:28,070 --> 01:37:29,880
It was incredible.

1949
01:37:29,880 --> 01:37:30,947
- [Joel] There's deep purple right now.

1950
01:37:30,947 --> 01:37:33,930
You see how they're using
that deep purple on there?

1951
01:37:33,930 --> 01:37:35,430
- [Crow] Oh, very psychedelic.

1952
01:37:36,620 --> 01:37:37,553
Almost funkadelic.

1953
01:37:38,550 --> 01:37:41,450
- [Joel] Yeah, it was a
confunktion of sorts, I would say.

1954
01:37:43,500 --> 01:37:45,090
And do you think he had a thing going

1955
01:37:45,090 --> 01:37:47,153
with Atlanta or was it with Marina?

1956
01:37:48,810 --> 01:37:49,690
- [Crow] It could be both.

1957
01:37:49,690 --> 01:37:52,400
He was kind of a underwater stud.

1958
01:37:52,400 --> 01:37:53,770
- [Joel] He was.

1959
01:37:53,770 --> 01:37:55,760
- [Crow] Well, I'm gonna go
clean up the main control room.

1960
01:37:55,760 --> 01:37:57,170
- Okay, I'll meet you back over there.

1961
01:37:57,170 --> 01:37:58,614
Here we go, let's get outta here.

1962
01:37:58,614 --> 01:38:01,364
(dramatic music)

1963
01:38:28,244 --> 01:38:31,472
(dramatic music)

1964
01:38:31,472 --> 01:38:34,139
(doors closing)

1965
01:38:40,080 --> 01:38:40,913
All right.

1966
01:38:40,913 --> 01:38:42,110
What did you think of that movie?

1967
01:38:42,110 --> 01:38:42,950
I kinda liked it.

1968
01:38:42,950 --> 01:38:44,900
In fact, I'm expecting
a lot of great things

1969
01:38:44,900 --> 01:38:46,260
to come from Troy Tempest.

1970
01:38:46,260 --> 01:38:49,413
Like, I think his distinctive
walk could really catch on.

1971
01:38:54,350 --> 01:38:55,343
Think I got it?

1972
01:38:56,350 --> 01:38:58,550
Well, anyway, one thing
I wanted to tell you

1973
01:38:58,550 --> 01:39:01,240
before you went is thanks
a lot for joining me

1974
01:39:01,240 --> 01:39:03,820
here on "Mystery Science Theater 3000,"

1975
01:39:03,820 --> 01:39:05,960
and that if you pay
attention to the number

1976
01:39:05,960 --> 01:39:07,880
that's being flashed on your screen,

1977
01:39:07,880 --> 01:39:10,200
you can call me, if
everything works out okay,

1978
01:39:10,200 --> 01:39:12,100
you can call me up here at the satellite

1979
01:39:12,100 --> 01:39:13,160
and leave a message.

1980
01:39:13,160 --> 01:39:15,910
It should transmit, it's
something I kinda Jerry-rigged.

1981
01:39:15,910 --> 01:39:18,420
I'm not sure if it'll
work, but if you put in

1982
01:39:18,420 --> 01:39:20,920
a good response, maybe end up on the air

1983
01:39:20,920 --> 01:39:22,100
in a couple of weeks or something,

1984
01:39:22,100 --> 01:39:24,520
you might want to keep watching.

1985
01:39:24,520 --> 01:39:27,530
Anyway, I had one more invention
I wanted to show you, too.

1986
01:39:27,530 --> 01:39:30,080
This is a thing I made
for more people on Earth.

1987
01:39:30,080 --> 01:39:34,460
It's for a guy who would
happen to play bagpipes,

1988
01:39:34,460 --> 01:39:35,731
but they're electric.

1989
01:39:35,731 --> 01:39:39,340
(vacuum whirring)
(dissonant music)

1990
01:39:39,340 --> 01:39:41,860
The reason why I made this is so that

1991
01:39:41,860 --> 01:39:44,127
the guy could sing along
while he played, you know?

1992
01:39:44,127 --> 01:39:45,921
(vacuum whirring)
(dissonant music)

1993
01:39:45,921 --> 01:39:50,169
♪ Amazing grace ♪

1994
01:39:50,169 --> 01:39:53,115
♪ How sweet ♪

1995
01:39:53,115 --> 01:39:55,737
♪ The sound ♪

1996
01:39:55,737 --> 01:39:57,150
♪ That ♪

1997
01:39:57,150 --> 01:39:59,767
I can also do Led Zepplin tunes.

1998
01:39:59,767 --> 01:40:00,923
♪ She's got a whole lotta love ♪

1999
01:40:00,923 --> 01:40:02,162
(vacuum whirring)
(dissonant music)

2000
01:40:02,162 --> 01:40:04,650
♪ A whole lotta love ♪

2001
01:40:04,650 --> 01:40:07,007
♪ She's got a whole lotta love ♪

2002
01:40:07,007 --> 01:40:10,090
♪ A whole lotta love ♪

2003
01:40:12,427 --> 01:40:15,030
- Bravissimo, bravo, bravo.

2004
01:40:15,030 --> 01:40:16,420
- Oh, thanks, Crow.

2005
01:40:16,420 --> 01:40:18,520
- Might I say that that
was an amazingly beautiful

2006
01:40:18,520 --> 01:40:19,990
performance on the bagpipe.
- Thanks.

2007
01:40:19,990 --> 01:40:21,230
I'm glad you liked it.

2008
01:40:21,230 --> 01:40:23,250
- The walk was very nice as well.

2009
01:40:23,250 --> 01:40:24,590
- Wow, thanks.

2010
01:40:24,590 --> 01:40:26,200
You know, everything's worked out okay

2011
01:40:26,200 --> 01:40:28,620
since we had that epidemic
of that strange foam

2012
01:40:28,620 --> 01:40:33,050
from outer space, you know,
Gypsy's out sky munching

2013
01:40:33,050 --> 01:40:36,420
on the spiral on down,
I got over my sickness,

2014
01:40:36,420 --> 01:40:38,370
I'm doing okay.

2015
01:40:38,370 --> 01:40:41,810
You know, everything's
worked out all right.

2016
01:40:41,810 --> 01:40:43,430
- Yes, it has.

2017
01:40:43,430 --> 01:40:45,440
I wonder what it was, though.

2018
01:40:45,440 --> 01:40:47,650
Maybe it was an unknowable,
but important gesture

2019
01:40:47,650 --> 01:40:51,670
in the grand scheme of
things, you know, God blinked?

2020
01:40:51,670 --> 01:40:52,862
- Hmm.

2021
01:40:52,862 --> 01:40:53,695
Nah.

2022
01:40:53,695 --> 01:40:56,800
- Or maybe the virus
was a biological misfit,

2023
01:40:56,800 --> 01:40:58,010
and like the Andromeda strain,

2024
01:40:58,010 --> 01:41:00,960
became inert and eventually
blew over the Eastern seaboard.

2025
01:41:01,810 --> 01:41:04,163
- Interesting idea, but I don't think so.

2026
01:41:05,010 --> 01:41:06,100
- Hmm.

2027
01:41:06,100 --> 01:41:07,150
Joel?

2028
01:41:07,150 --> 01:41:08,260
- Yeah, Crow.

2029
01:41:08,260 --> 01:41:10,620
- Did you ever wonder
that maybe this spaceship

2030
01:41:10,620 --> 01:41:12,010
isn't really a spaceship at all,

2031
01:41:12,010 --> 01:41:14,220
but a television set
built for the amusement

2032
01:41:14,220 --> 01:41:16,670
of the viewing audience,
and I'm not really a robot,

2033
01:41:16,670 --> 01:41:18,620
but a puppet built to look like a robot,

2034
01:41:18,620 --> 01:41:20,010
who is in reality being controlled

2035
01:41:20,010 --> 01:41:22,540
by a puppeteer under this very table.

2036
01:41:22,540 --> 01:41:25,510
And you're not a scientist/inventor
trapped in outer space,

2037
01:41:25,510 --> 01:41:28,070
but just a comedian playing
a part on a television show

2038
01:41:28,070 --> 01:41:28,953
that you wrote.

2039
01:41:29,866 --> 01:41:30,699
- Hmm.

2040
01:41:31,550 --> 01:41:33,350
No, I don't think so either.

2041
01:41:33,350 --> 01:41:34,293
Somehow.

2042
01:41:35,260 --> 01:41:38,500
You know, Crow, one thing
I always wanted to ask you

2043
01:41:38,500 --> 01:41:40,630
is why is it that you never foam?

2044
01:41:40,630 --> 01:41:41,960
- Because I thought I'd save it

2045
01:41:41,960 --> 01:41:43,690
for the end of our transmission.

2046
01:41:43,690 --> 01:41:44,703
- Oh, great idea.

2047
01:41:47,520 --> 01:41:48,460
You serious?

2048
01:41:48,460 --> 01:41:49,613
Golly, ick.

2049
01:41:51,110 --> 01:41:52,260
I guess that's it, folks.

2050
01:41:52,260 --> 01:41:54,030
We'll see ya.

2051
01:41:54,030 --> 01:41:55,300
You are sick.

2052
01:41:55,300 --> 01:41:56,133
- Goodbye.

